{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition","id":1293163,"title":"Choosing Tradition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-01T15:34:50-08:00","id":1293163,"title":"Choosing Tradition","content":"Hi Which standards you normally follow to choose your character tradition? Do you go by her nature/demeanor/concept? Her practices and beliefs? Her character sheet and sphere dots?<br /> <br /> I am thinking which would be the best tradition to fit a character that follows those descriptions:<br /> <br /> He is(was) and engineer/scientist before awakening, who values his physical development as much as his mental. He is very determined and competitive, even a little bit egoistic and sometimes aggressive. Before awakening his goals were to perfect his body and his mind. He did that by working out and practicing martial arts to get the best of his physical abilities, and meditating/studying to keep his mind sharp, always eager for more knowledge. <br /> After his awake, one more goal was added to his list: to obtain more magickal power and knowledge as possible. Now he has three fronts, three aspects of his life that he wishes to develop.<br /> <br /> I had in mind some Order of Hermes house or Akashic. Going by his personality, I would say he's and hermetic. He doesn't care about any dogma or religion, he cares only for his improvement. Having said that, I would say one of those 3 houses: Tytalus, because of his strong will and desire to improve; Flambeau, because of his agressiveness and his practices (I'll cover that later); or Bonisagus, because of his thirst for knowledge and magickal power.<br /> <br /> Now, going by his practices, he`d fit more an akashic, since most of he would use martial arts and psyionics as practices, and most of his instruments would be about his body or mind (gestures, meditation, energy, etc.), but he definitely isn't asian or cares for anything they teach and follows. His selfishness wouldn't go well in this tradition.<br /> <br /> By his concept he could be an etherite because of his scientific past, but I think this is not enough.<br /> <br /> What you guys think? Tell me if more info is needed. Also, feel free to post examples of how you decide your tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T16:08:25-08:00","id":1293177,"title":"","content":"<b>Concept</b> it's the key. While it hasn't any mechanical advantage I think that Concept it's one of the most important lines of the Character Sheet as it's basically asking the player to describe in a short line what he wants to play. Everything else aligns either alone or with a little shove.<br /> <br /> With that character and aspirations he would make a great Tytalus, but if SCIENCE! it's his call theres no reason whatsoever to think that an Etherite can't care about self perfection more than anything else: In fact, I invite you to read, if you have it, the writeup of &quot;<b>Invigoration</b>&quot; in Book of Secrets. It's a primarily Etherite Practice, practiced by luminaries like Doc Eon (a great martial artist) and it's basically your character. In a short resume: It's a Practice based arround the idea that both the body and the mind have a hidden potential that can be unlocked to do incredible, seemingly superhumaan, stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-01-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T16:26:02-08:00","id":1293181,"title":"","content":"Agreed.<br /> <br /> Concept is definitely the most important, because Traditions offer very little besides an idea of how you want to express all of the other character aspects discussed. A Tytalan Hermetic, an Adventurer Etherite, and a aggressive Akashayana can all have very similar looking sheets, Focus, and so on, but the stories implied by how they come to terms with their Tradition's teachings are going to be very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T18:54:57-08:00","id":1293216,"title":"","content":"Concept, and what seems interesting to me at the time. <br /> <br /> What you describe would work equally well as a Hermetic (House Tytalus most likely, but some of the others would also work), the Akashic Brotherhood (Li Hai or ShiRen spring to mind), and the Sons of Ether (the traditional Doc Savage scientific superman archetype). I could probably also make it work as a Verbena, Thanatoic, Virtual Adept and Hollow One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T23:52:05-08:00","id":1293248,"title":"","content":"Concept is god.<br /> <br /> It really comes down to &quot;Okay, I've done for casting magic, x, y, and z, what haven't I done? How about h?&quot;, building from there, and then spiraling both ways to figure out why I think h changes the world and seeing which Tradition fulfills h.<br /> <br /> Ascension is about the power and logic that lies behind aesthetic. I pick an image for conveying power that is fun for me and then go from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T07:26:30-08:00","id":1293291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition#post1293163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By his concept he could be an etherite because of his scientific past, but I think this is not enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the issues I think you are running into is that this isn't a concept. This is a backstory. What does he believe now? What best explains the universe for him now? Answer those and you should have much more understanding of how he approaches martial arts and psionics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T10:04:24-08:00","id":1293308,"title":"","content":"Even that he is a scientist, he doesn't practice &quot;Science!&quot;. After awakening, he became a scholar of the unknown, a scientist of the nature of magick. But he does acknowledge it as magick. That's another reason OoH might be a good idea, and why Bonisagus is on the list.<br /> <br /> But his focus looks more like an akashic. He believes that magick is basically the manipulation of energy and the best way to do it is through your body and your Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T03:32:00-08:00","id":1293439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition#post1293163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Which standards you normally follow to choose your character tradition? Do you go by her nature/demeanor/concept? Her practices and beliefs? Her character sheet and sphere dots?<br /> <br /> I am thinking which would be the best tradition to fit a character that follows those descriptions:<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> What you guys think? Tell me if more info is needed. Also, feel free to post examples of how you decide your tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this character concept would fit for a member of House Tytalus most. This is because he is ambitious and seeks constant self-improvement in several areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-03T16:01:10-08:00","id":1293561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1293308#post1293308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even that he is a scientist, he doesn't practice &quot;Science!&quot;. After awakening, he became a scholar of the unknown, a scientist of the nature of magick. But he does acknowledge it as magick. That's another reason OoH might be a good idea, and why Bonisagus is on the list.<br /> <br /> But his focus looks more like an akashic. He believes that magick is basically the manipulation of energy and the best way to do it is through your body and your Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically this could still go all three ways, but I'd say OoH is the best fit.<br /> <br /> While he does put focus on the flow of energy through his body, much like an Akashic would, he is more interested in studying what is happening and not on where he is going. While he studies things scientifically, like an Etherite, he considers himself part of the magic not a separate entity. OoH respects the academic studying of magic, the concept of Will, and is open enough to strange forms of Magic if they can be put in those terms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T08:47:53-08:00","id":1294071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1293561#post1293561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically this could still go all three ways, but I'd say OoH is the best fit.<br /> <br /> While he does put focus on the flow of energy through his body, much like an Akashic would, he is more interested in studying what is happening and not on where he is going. While he studies things scientifically, like an Etherite, he considers himself part of the magic not a separate entity. OoH respects the academic studying of magic, the concept of Will, and is open enough to strange forms of Magic if they can be put in those terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You gor it exactly right. He could be either 3, but seems to go better as hermetic. Now would be nice to choose the best house.<br /> As I posted before, the scholar aspect of this char would probably be welcomed in the Bonisagus house, although they seem to focus too much on high magick and I don't know how they accept other forms of practices.<br /> House Tytalus seems a good choice for all the reasons already pointed. <br /> Now, I would like to try to fit him into house flambeau. He is kinda agressive and is combat focused, with dots in martial arts, fire arms and melee. Also, flambeau seems to be the house where his practices would be more accepted. And there is the badass factor of the house that I'd like the char to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T09:21:58-08:00","id":1294085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294071#post1294071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You gor it exactly right. He could be either 3, but seems to go better as hermetic. Now would be nice to choose the best house.<br /> As I posted before, the scholar aspect of this char would probably be welcomed in the Bonisagus house, although they seem to focus too much on high magick and I don't know how they accept other forms of practices.<br /> House Tytalus seems a good choice for all the reasons already pointed.<br /> Now, I would like to try to fit him into house flambeau. He is kinda agressive and is combat focused, with dots in martial arts, fire arms and melee. Also, flambeau seems to be the house where his practices would be more accepted. And there is the badass factor of the house that I'd like the char to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>If House Flambeau is where you would like him to be, then put him there. I think you've just given more than enough reason to justify that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T09:40:40-08:00","id":1294091,"title":"","content":"I always think of what I want to play first, and then build my concept around that. Technically, I suspect in oWoD most awakened people join the first faction to pick them up, regardless of personality/education/profession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T08:02:00-08:00","id":1294400,"title":"","content":"I see. I thought the houses and traditions would be more restrict about tje mage beliefs and foci, I think.<br /> There is anorher source of information about the houses besides the hermetic tradition book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T08:16:00-08:00","id":1294405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1293308#post1293308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even that he is a scientist, he doesn't practice &quot;Science!&quot;. After awakening, he became a scholar of the unknown, a scientist of the nature of magick. But he does acknowledge it as magick. That's another reason OoH might be a good idea, and why Bonisagus is on the list.<br /> <br /> But his focus looks more like an akashic. He believes that magick is basically the manipulation of energy and the best way to do it is through your body and your Will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scientific Mystic is a thing. There are plenty of Etherites who actively consider the wall between &quot;science and Magic&quot; to just be Technocratic propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:06:54-08:00","id":1294443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294400#post1294400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. I thought the houses and traditions would be more restrict about tje mage beliefs and foci, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much. In general, a Tradition's philosophy, beliefs and paradigm are more about <i>why</i> the foci, tools and rituals work rather than exactly what they should be. At least this is the way 1st, 2nd and Revised editions were set up; I've no idea about M20 specifics. (And yes, there are also cultural considerations as well.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is anorher source of information about the houses besides the hermetic tradition book? </div> </div> </div>The Order of Hermes originated in the game Ars Magica, and have been the subject of several sourcebooks over that game's long history. The 2nd ed book Order of Hermes, the 3rd ed book Houses of Hermes, and the most recent and most in depth 5th edition trilogy Houses of Hermes: Mystery Cults (Bjornaer, Criamon, Merinita, Verditius), Houses of Hermes: Societies (Flambeau, Jerbiton, Tytalus, Ex Misc), and Houses of Hermes: True Lineages (Bonisagus, Guernicus, Mercere, Tremere). Ars Magica's history is a bit different from that of Mage and the World of Darkness (the founder of the Tremere having died several decades ago and them still being part of the Order is just the start), and the rules systems are radically different, but the information about their philosophies, mindsets and structure are still useful. You can find PDF copies of Ars Magica books at the <a href=\"http://www.warehouse23.com\" target=\"_blank\">Warehouse23</a> online store. (Of the books, I've found the three 5th edition ones the most useful, and the 3rd edition one probably the least useful of the group.)<br /> <br /> The more modern Houses only appear in the Tradition books, but House Solificati was originally the Mage: Sorcerers' Crusade Tradition of alchemists which briefly held the Seat of Matter. After collapsing, they became the Children of Knowledge Craft detailed in the Book of Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 03-06-2019, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T10:09:04-08:00","id":1294444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294085#post1294085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If House Flambeau is where you would like him to be, then put him there. I think you've just given more than enough reason to justify that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the mentioned rising stars of House Flambeau in the original Tradition book was a Russian nuclear physicist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:48:54-08:00","id":1294737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294405#post1294405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Scientific Mystic is a thing. There are plenty of Etherites who actively consider the wall between &amp;quot;science and Magic&amp;quot; to just be Technocratic propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you got me thinking. But I see the Etherites as a bunch of phds that reunite to discuss scientific discoveries and public papers. I don't see them as much as a tradition. I'll read the tradition book again though. <br /> <br /> Also, my char is a scientist, but not a phd, i think his curriculum is not enough to be in the society, and his methods would be probably be seen as a joke. Martial arta and psionics aren't quite the practices etherites likes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T08:28:27-08:00","id":1294750,"title":"","content":"Yes they are. Etherites are nowhere close to 'real science'. Etherites are just as likely to use Orgonne generators (AkA generating electrical power via having sex with a weird box at the foot of the bed) and accupuncture as they are to use physics.<br /> <br /> They approach everything scientifically yes. But they go in with the assumption that EVERYTHING is true. Meaning martial arts and psionics are just as true as anything else.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like to think of paradigm as 'what is this characters superhero origin story? How do their powers work and how did they get them?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T17:13:34-08:00","id":1294929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294737#post1294737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you got me thinking. But I see the Etherites as a bunch of phds that reunite to discuss scientific discoveries and public papers. I don't see them as much as a tradition. I'll read the tradition book again though.<br /> <br /> Also, my char is a scientist, but not a phd, i think his curriculum is not enough to be in the society, and his methods would be probably be seen as a joke. Martial arta and psionics aren't quite the practices etherites likes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's one aspect of them. But there are Adventurers for example who go off the deep but generally the difference between the Technocratic and Etherite Paradigm is a matter of inclusion. The Technocratic Paradigm is... ironically BAD science. It presets the results and works backwards &quot;We want x how do we get there&quot; and forces everything out. The Etherites rather see &quot;ok Kung Fu Works so.. how does it work..&quot; then they come up with a theory and test it. Martial arts and Psionics are DEFINATELY practices the Etherites like and there is a whole Merit you can take to double your Practices to mix in full on crazy shit like having Wierd Science and Shamanism..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:21:17-08:00","id":1294938,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, the Technocracy is about control, not science. Science and technology are just means to an end, the same way religion was for the Cabal of Pure Thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T20:53:23-08:00","id":1294965,"title":"","content":"To choose which tradition would fit better, I believe it all comes to how the mage sees and explains what he is doing.<br /> I'm trying to think what would be the difference of an hermetic scientist and an etherite adventurer trying to explain an effect like creating lightning from his body energy and directing through his hands. Or meditating and breathing until his whiole body turn into fire. I guess, since both have a scientific mind, the explanations would be quite similar. What would be the difference since one is a mystic and the other a technomancer? One is doing magick and the other Science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T22:04:21-08:00","id":1294971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294965#post1294965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To choose which tradition would fit better, I believe it all comes to how the mage sees and explains what he is doing.<br /> I'm trying to think what would be the difference of an hermetic scientist and an etherite adventurer trying to explain an effect like creating lightning from his body energy and directing through his hands. Or meditating and breathing until his whiole body turn into fire. I guess, since both have a scientific mind, the explanations would be quite similar. What would be the difference since one is a mystic and the other a technomancer? One is doing magick and the other Science?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Etherites will frequently employ fringe or discredited sciences as part of their praxis. And if we're talking about defunct science that lets you manipulate electricity in the body, you'd be hard pressed to find one more on the money that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_magnetism\" target=\"_blank\">Animal Magnetism</a>.<br /> <br /> It's a theory and practice that revolved around manipulating &quot;vital fluids&quot; in the body through the magnetic fields that all living things possess. It's inventor, Franz Mesmer, promoted it as a method for healing (by running magnets or even just one's hands over a patient's body). But proponents of the theory (&quot;Magnetizers&quot; or &quot;Mesmerists&quot;) claimed to be able to use it for all sorts of tasks. Like levitating objects, conjuring objects, communing with the dead, mind control (especially from great distances), and the like.<br /> <br /> I've insisted in the past on this forum that plenty of Etherites are likely to employ Animal Magnetism. Using it to shoot lightning from one's hands is totally on brand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:34:01-08:00","id":1295014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1294965#post1294965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To choose which tradition would fit better, I believe it all comes to how the mage sees and explains what he is doing.<br /> I'm trying to think what would be the difference of an hermetic scientist and an etherite adventurer trying to explain an effect like creating lightning from his body energy and directing through his hands. Or meditating and breathing until his whiole body turn into fire. I guess, since both have a scientific mind, the explanations would be quite similar. What would be the difference since one is a mystic and the other a technomancer? One is doing magick and the other Science?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The biggest difference is that the vast majority of the time the Etherite is going to think of what he is doing as external and the Hermetic is going to think of the effect as internal. I don't mean that in the sense of happening inside or outside the body, I mean that the Etherite doesn't think he's part of the Magic/Science and the Hermetic does.<br /> <br /> For the Etherites effects are based on external scientific (Or Scientific!) principles that, in theory, could happen without them. Their enlightened minds let them see and calculate the necessary actions to make them happen on command, but they aren't a vital component of the effect. That's part of why Etherites have a hard time dropping foci; they can't internalize something that isn't internal.<br /> <br /> While the Hermetics are just as interested in researching the fundamental forces of the universe they also include an Awakened Will as a necessary component of any effect. Someone without that Will could try to perform the ritual moves for as long as they like, with 100% accuracy, and they still wouldn't accomplish anything because they don't understand what they are doing.<br /> <br /> The Etherites think their effects require an fundamental enlightenment to understand, the Hermetics think their effects require a fundamental enlightenment to do.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-08-2019, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T07:36:36-08:00","id":1295044,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> That's pretty cool! It is exactly something my char would believe and use. Something like that being achieved through martial arts and psionics.<br /> But both the Etherite and the hermetic could believe in something like this. <br /> I find very hard to differentiate paradigms of mages using the same practices. Well, maybe there is no need to be differences, since both think scientifically.. But myatic vs technomancer is still a confusion to me.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> How is the Etherite not a vital component of the when it happens in his body?<br /> Looks like both think their effect needs enlightenment to be cast, but the hermetic include Will and the Etherite doesn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T09:34:00-08:00","id":1295068,"title":"","content":"I was reading the entry of martial arts in M20 and noticed this part about technomancers using this practice:<br /> <br /> &quot;Although she couldn\u2019t fly through the air or skip along tree branches by manipulating chi (\u201cThat\u2019s just mythology!\u201d), she can still rework conventional physics and biology through her understanding of the fighting arts.&quot; <br /> <br /> So, maybe a technomancer is more limited in his effects without a special gadget to explain it. While the hermetic could still explain scientifically, when he adds his Will(or amy other mystic explanation) to the equation he can cast effects like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T10:17:00-08:00","id":1295075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295044#post1295044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> How is the Etherite not a vital component of the when it happens in his body?<br /> Looks like both think their effect needs enlightenment to be cast, but the hermetic include Will and the Etherite doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a different meaning of the word 'internal.' Yes, both mages are using an effect that is at least partially within their bodies. Only one of them thinks that she is a necessary component of the spell. <br /> <br /> Let's use a different effect for the moment. Lets say both a Hermetic and an Etherite decide to knock down a wall with force. Let's also say the Hermetic uses a staff inscribed with runes and the Etherite uses some kind of ray gun. In both cases the spell is physically external to the mage, originating in an object and projecting towards another object. The Hermetic, though, would still argue that her Enlightened Will was a necessary component of the spell and it could not have happened without her. In contrast the Etherite would say his effect was based on impartial principles that exist whether he is there or not, he just had the Enlightenment to understand and make use of them. <br /> <br /> To put it yet another way, the Hermetic is causing something to happen, the Etherite is doing something that causes something else to happen.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Intrinsic vs Extrinsic would be better terms than Internal vs External. Let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T12:11:02-08:00","id":1295103,"title":"","content":"Interestingly enough, actual, Real World medieval Hermetics would be in accord with the fictional Etherites. Old literature on the subject of magic from that era approached magic as a kind of Natural Philosophy, the precursor to what we in modern times would call &quot;Science&quot;. The Greek and Roman philosophers believed in an understandable universe, with explicable laws of nature. Medieval occultists followed suit (because of course they'd put stock in Classical thinkers implicitly), and wrote of magic in the sense of it being the understanding of natural laws. It's just that their laws included things like the Laws of Sympathy, Antipathy, Humorism, Contagion, Spontaneous Generation, and the inherent, mystical properties of stones, herbs, and metals. Even the calling of spirits, demons, and angels was merely an exercise in exploiting divine wisdom revealed to mankind.<br /> <br /> It's only much later that Aleister Crowley came up with the idea of the &quot;True Will&quot;, and made magic(k) more a function of willworking than mere knowledge. The writers of Mage: The Ascension (and possibly also Ars Magica) then back-ported this idea, so it retroactively &quot;always&quot; was was medieval Hermetics believed in-universe. There is a LOT of what these two games owe to the syncretisms pioneered by the Golden Dawn and later writers, when it comes to the conception of Hermeticism.<br /> <br /> That said, as it stands now, in MtAs, Hermetic rituals and tools are at least in some respect a means by which the magician focuses their Will. Hence why their magick is Intrinsic to them, allowing for the more rapid overcoming of Instruments than an Etherite can, with his Extrinsic understanding of magick (or Science!). The Etherite believes that his body-lightning works because that's just a part of the physical laws of the universe, that could theoretically be used by anyone if they just studied enough.<br /> <br /> <i>Technically</i>, he's not exactly wrong. Sorcerers are a thing that exist, and are capable of using their Linear arts without Enlightenment. It's just that this approach also holds back the Awakened scientist when he's trying to overcome the need for his tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T15:21:36-08:00","id":1295136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295075#post1295075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a different meaning of the word 'internal.' Yes, both mages are using an effect that is at least partially within their bodies. Only one of them thinks that she is a necessary component of the spell.<br /> <br /> Let's use a different effect for the moment. Lets say both a Hermetic and an Etherite decide to knock down a wall with force. Let's also say the Hermetic uses a staff inscribed with runes and the Etherite uses some kind of ray gun. In both cases the spell is physically external to the mage, originating in an object and projecting towards another object. The Hermetic, though, would still argue that her Enlightened Will was a necessary component of the spell and it could not have happened without her. In contrast the Etherite would say his effect was based on impartial principles that exist whether he is there or not, he just had the Enlightenment to understand and make use of them.<br /> <br /> To put it yet another way, the Hermetic is causing something to happen, the Etherite is doing something that causes something else to happen.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Intrinsic vs Extrinsic would be better terms than Internal vs External. Let me know what you think.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> too:<br /> <br /> I understand and I agree. The Will is the key here. The hermetic believes his Will is what is actually doing the effect, while the etherite believes that is just plain physics of the universe doing its thing when he activates the ray gun. I got it. But this leaves to another problem. In this case, if the etherite lends his ray gun to a sleeper, technically the sleeper should be able to cast the effect, since is just activating the gun and there is no need for an enlightened Will. Maybe technomancers effects shouldn't be so simple as pulling a trigger on a gun and hence sleepers can't do it (unless the technomancer builds a gun this simple in the form of a wonder, which could be used by the sleeper)... I don't know.<br /> <br /> This also made me think about my post about technomancers and the martial arts practice. Maybe technomancers cannot use some effects at all without a external apparatus. How could a technomancer explain turning his body into a dog with meditation??<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T17:13:52-08:00","id":1295159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295136#post1295136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> too:<br /> <br /> I understand and I agree. The Will is the key here. The hermetic believes his Will is what is actually doing the effect, while the etherite believes that is just plain physics of the universe doing its thing when he activates the ray gun. I got it. But this leaves to another problem. In this case, if the etherite lends his ray gun to a sleeper, technically the sleeper should be able to cast the effect, since is just activating the gun and there is no need for an enlightened Will. Maybe technomancers effects shouldn't be so simple as pulling a trigger on a gun and hence sleepers can't do it (unless the technomancer builds a gun this simple in the form of a wonder, which could be used by the sleeper)... I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The hand-wavy explanation is probably the only one we really have: you'd be surprised how difficult using a ray gun could be.<br /> <br /> I mean that in the sense that the Etherite would probably explain it as the ray gun being more complicated or finicky than it would first appear. &quot;You have to know what you're doing&quot;, they might say. Whether it's a selection of knobs that's needed to calibrate the machine (remember, the ray gun is an Instrument to be used for a broad range of Effects, not just a single-use zappy gun). Or it's considered a &quot;prototype&quot;, so one needs to handle it correctly.<br /> <br /> And of course a Sleeper CAN &quot;know what they're doing&quot;...if they've invested in the proper Sorcery knowledge. Probably Path of Hellfire. The Technocrats have a similar angle with their Extraordinary Citizens. You don't expect lab technicians to not be trained in the high level sciences the Union is working with, eh?<br /> <br /> Yes, it's kind of a cop-out argument - that all the Instruments technomancers use immediately fail in the hands of normies, because they don't get how to operate them. But then again, if the machines were intuitive enough to employ by the layman, they'd be Devices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also made me think about my post about technomancers and the martial arts practice. Maybe technomancers cannot use some effects at all without a external apparatus. How could a technomancer explain turning his body into a dog with meditation?? </div> </div> </div>Technomancers differ from mystics in that they believe that Instruments have a value unto themselves, independent of the Will of the caster. Martial arts, meditation, and even co-opted ancient artifacts all obviously have power. It's up to the technomancer to create a theory for it. Even if that theory has &quot;psychic powers&quot; somewhere in there.<br /> <br /> A technomancer might subscribe to neuro-linguistic programming, to explain that his tight focus upon the form of a canine could cause his body to reorder itself. Basically a combination of self-hypnosis and a juiced up Placebo Effect. Body Control is such an established part of Reality that it's a mundane Ability, rather than any sort of hedge magic, so an Etherite would be well within his rights to question just how far a human's mutability can be stretched.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the technomancer might have previously fiddled with his own DNA, laying in a series of functions that lie dormant. Until he uses mental exercises to release the proper cocktail of hormones, that trigger the dormant function, inducing change into a dog. Moreover, that same technomancer may believe his theory is borne out by the existence of the changing breeds, who &quot;must have a naturally occurring genetic predisposition towards changing shape&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i>Alternatively</i> alternatively, the technomancer could pull a Miracle Man, and be employing meditation to draw upon a quantum-displaced version of himself, as a dog, from another dimension.<br /> <br /> Or still more alternatively, the technomancer could be a Virtual Adept who employs Reality Hacking. Changing into a dog is as easy as editing their own &quot;file&quot; in the grand simulation that is the observable universe, changing them from &quot;Human&quot; to &quot;Canine&quot;. The meditation is simply one method of accessing this data. Whether because they've &quot;programmed&quot; their brains to emulate a computer operating system (a neat idea I stole from Serial Experiments Lain), or because they just think that, data being data, thought is no less a viable strategy for interfacing with the simulation as any computer. The &quot;meditation&quot; part is simply them needing to focus really hard on the exact mental inputs needed to accomplish their goal (hence why they aren't &quot;casting without Instruments&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-08-2019, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T07:29:46-08:00","id":1295308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295136#post1295136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> too:<br /> <br /> I understand and I agree. The Will is the key here. The hermetic believes his Will is what is actually doing the effect, while the etherite believes that is just plain physics of the universe doing its thing when he activates the ray gun. I got it. But this leaves to another problem. In this case, if the etherite lends his ray gun to a sleeper, technically the sleeper should be able to cast the effect, since is just activating the gun and there is no need for an enlightened Will. Maybe technomancers effects shouldn't be so simple as pulling a trigger on a gun and hence sleepers can't do it (unless the technomancer builds a gun this simple in the form of a wonder, which could be used by the sleeper)... I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are clear cases in the books of mages being able to 'cast' without realizing they are casting. Technocrats can sometimes cause physical effects (like stairs collapsing) by 'observing' relevant details (those stairs look structurally compromised), and 'predicting' the results (I think they are going to collapse right about... now). Chakravanti sometimes reap the benefits of being in alignment with the wheel without ever intending something to happen. To put it in systems terms, the Player is clearly describing an effect, naming the Spheres, and making an Arete roll, but the Character is unaware he is doing anything at all.<br /> <br /> For that reason, I would absolutely allow the player of an Etherite to make an Arete roll to cause an effect when a sleeper uses his gear in his presence. So yes, scenes where an Etherite tosses a bystander his raygun and tells them to shoot the charging mutant-cyber-death-gorilla could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also made me think about my post about technomancers and the martial arts practice. Maybe technomancers cannot use some effects at all without a external apparatus. How could a technomancer explain turning his body into a dog with meditation?? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> has already handled this well. Instruments don't have to be physical. The very fact that psionics can fit into a Technocratic or Technomantic paradigm shows that nonphysical (or naturally occuring organic) instruments are possible so long as the 'science' in question has a reason for them to be. Changing human flesh in to dog flesh isn't any more mind blowing than turning human flesh as hard as steel or controlling fire with your mind. Even if it were, there have been some really strange scientific theories over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T11:28:32-08:00","id":1295357,"title":"","content":"I see. But the explanations were just too crazy and with other effects they could be even more. Now, according to the entry I quoted, technomancer should not be able to pull things like that. But i went to read the sidebar Science! In M20 pg290 and there it is said that if the explanation given by the scientist is too crazy, then it vulgar magick.<br /> <br /> Now I don't know if he shouldn't be able to cast or just cast as vulgar, since no one would believe in neuro longuistic programing to turn into a dog.<br /> Maybe the sidebar works for technomancer and mu quote were for technocrats. They do have a harder time with mysticism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T00:08:08-08:00","id":1295516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295159#post1295159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, it's kind of a cop-out argument - that all the Instruments technomancers use immediately fail in the hands of normies, because they don't get how to operate them. But then again, if the machines were intuitive enough to employ by the layman, they'd be Devices.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyone who says &quot;Its a copout&quot; needs to do more tech Support for old people. &quot;I can't figure out how to save files!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T04:24:29-07:00","id":1295754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295357#post1295357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. But the explanations were just too crazy and with other effects they could be even more. Now, according to the entry I quoted, technomancer should not be able to pull things like that. But i went to read the sidebar Science! In M20 pg290 and there it is said that if the explanation given by the scientist is too crazy, then it vulgar magick.<br /> <br /> Now I don't know if he shouldn't be able to cast or just cast as vulgar, since no one would believe in neuro longuistic programing to turn into a dog.<br /> Maybe the sidebar works for technomancer and mu quote were for technocrats. They do have a harder time with mysticism</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yes, turning yourself into a dog is definitely vulgar in most places, regardless of the explanation. I'd still let Etherites do it if they had a reason in their paradigm. It probably shouldn't be the same explanation as an Akashic would use, but there's no reason a Technomancer couldn't have a martial arts style that let them transform or do wire work like effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T05:56:45-07:00","id":1295777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295357#post1295357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. But the explanations were just too crazy and with other effects they could be even more. Now, according to the entry I quoted, technomancer should not be able to pull things like that. But i went to read the sidebar Science! In M20 pg290 and there it is said that if the explanation given by the scientist is too crazy, then it vulgar magick.<br /> <br /> Now I don't know if he shouldn't be able to cast or just cast as vulgar, since no one would believe in neuro longuistic programing to turn into a dog.<br /> Maybe the sidebar works for technomancer and mu quote were for technocrats. They do have a harder time with mysticism</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No one believes you can turn into a dog period. Its Going to be vulgar Most places. Neurolinguistic hacking is probably an inappropriate practice for using with Life(the sphere needed to turn into a dog) In theory the game doesn't stop you but realistically there's what makes sense for the table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:00:36-07:00","id":1295818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295754#post1295754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh yes, turning yourself into a dog is definitely vulgar in most places, regardless of the explanation. I'd still let Etherites do it if they had a reason in their paradigm. It probably shouldn't be the same explanation as an Akashic would use, but there's no reason a Technomancer couldn't have a martial arts style that let them transform or do wire work like effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. But M20 have some entries where it says that using Science to cast some effects can't be done.<br /> There will always be an explanation, but for some effects, with some practices, unless you say &quot;because it's magic&quot; there won't be a reasonable one.<br /> <br /> See the examples given in this thread or the Science! sidebar in M20, even the Scientist wouldn't believe in such explanations. In this case I don't know if the effect is just vulgar or if it can't be done this way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T08:48:05-07:00","id":1295835,"title":"","content":"Those limitations you mention apply only to those that believe in such limitations, and they're more a question of fluff than rules.<br /> <br /> 1\u00ba<br /> <br /> The first example you gave isn't nearly as limiting as you make it to be:<br /> <br /> &quot;Although she couldn\u2019t fly through the air or skip along tree branches by manipulating chi (\u201cThat\u2019s just mythology!\u201d), she can still rework conventional physics and biology through her understanding of the fighting arts.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I can't use Chi but I can &quot;<i>rework conventional physics and biology through my understanding of the fighting arts&quot;</i>?<br /> <br /> OK: I rework gravity to nulify my weight and reverse asceleration <i>in order to fly trough the air and/or skip trough branches</i>. How it's that beyond &quot;reworking conventional physics&quot;...which apparently I can do with &quot;my figthing arts&quot;? There's very few things I can't do if I can &quot;rework conventional physics and biology&quot; with kung-fu...<br /> <br /> In other words:<br /> <br /> You're reading that paragraph like it's limiting what Science! can do, but in truth it's merely pointing out that Science! uses a different explanation to do exactly the same things<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that Scientific Mystics can believe in Chi, they will just think it's ancient science.<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba<br /> <br /> The sidebar it's confusing, I grant you that (and contradicts itself when it says that technomancers can't do certain things...then proceding to give rules to do literal &quot;handwavium&quot;). I don't like that sidebar, but it's understandable if you remember how Focus it's now divided in three parts.<br /> <br /> ALL mages have to explain how their magick works: While magick it's a very convinient explanation sometimes <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MagicAIsMagicA\" target=\"_blank\">Magic A is Magic A</a> and if a Chi user can't really explain how their approach to Chi and wuxia transforms them into a dog in a convincing way they can't do it...with that Instrument, but they may be able to do so if they have surpassed that Instrument or just decide to use the rules to cast w/o Instrument to work on Paradigm alone (If Reality is an Ilussion maybe I can be a dog...). Since Technomancers don't get to cast this way so easily M20 has a sidebar providing an alternative way (casting with a weird explanation).<br /> <br /> If you read that sidebar again you will notice that the explanation has to &quot;make sense&quot; to the technomancer...it doesn't have to &quot;be true&quot; nor to be reasonable from the pov of conventional science. It's a very light limitation that borders on none at all. It has even been debated than thanks to that sidebar M20 technomagick may be less limiting than mystic magick because mystics don't get to use &quot;handwavium&quot; when thay can't explain what they're doing...if this balances out with magick being a convinient explanation or not depends, really, on the imagination, knowledge (and sincerity) of the player...For instance, I don't think most Chi users turn into litaral animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-11-2019, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:02:56-07:00","id":1295841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295818#post1295818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. But M20 have some entries where it says that using Science to cast some effects can't be done.<br /> There will always be an explanation, but for some effects, with some practices, unless you say &quot;because it's magic&quot; there won't be a reasonable one.<br /> <br /> See the examples given in this thread or the Science! sidebar in M20, even the Scientist wouldn't believe in such explanations. In this case I don't know if the effect is just vulgar or if it can't be done this way</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the issue that you have a hard time envisioning a psuedo science that says a man can perform these feats with the right training or motions? Or is the issue that the book implies things that go that far are somehow not enough like Science?<br /> <br /> If it is the latter, I'm going to say ignore the book on this one, because there have been a lot of strange theories over the years that seem magical to us now but at the time were treated as real subjects of scientific inquiry (or at least as inquiry into the natural sciences). In Galileo's time it was believed that a drum made of lamb skin would not make a sound in the presence of a drum made of wolf skin. Lamark proposed that animals mutated over their lifetimes and could pass on those mutations. Within the last 200 years spontaneous generation was considered a valid explanation of how maggots formed.<br /> <br /> There really isn't a dividing line of strangeness where something stops being a science and starts being magic because some sciences were (and are) far, far stranger than magic. If the technomancer thinks he is operating of of strange natural laws or principles that allow an effect to happen, that's scientific enough to count. Even if it makes him sound like a character out of a comic book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T21:06:23-07:00","id":1296031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295835#post1295835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Although she couldn\u2019t fly through the air or skip along tree branches by manipulating chi (\u201cThat\u2019s just mythology!\u201d),</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except.. she might? I mean.. the Etherite book litterally covered how to incorporate Chi into A holistic SCIENTIFIC! understanding of the universe. She'd just have metric scale for measuring chi. And might incorporate that into cybernetics or have DBZ style scouters!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think most Chi users turn into litaral animals. </div> </div> </div>Spheres Matter. I think the fact that people are BROADLY more familiar with modern science than essoteric magical practices leads to a certain level of confusion. There are &quot;Different&quot; ways to use chi. The Techniques and &quot;Chi&quot; of flying and balancing on leaves Is different than punching someone into the opposite sex, both are part of the broad theory in the same way real science covers say medicine, airplanes are both a part of science but you wouldn't say apply aerospace engineering to fixing a broken leg. One should understand there are different specialties in magical practices that parallel broad divisions like science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T07:46:58-07:00","id":1296134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296031#post1296031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except.. she might? I mean.. the Etherite book litterally covered how to incorporate Chi into A holistic SCIENTIFIC! understanding of the universe. She'd just have metric scale for measuring chi. And might incorporate that into cybernetics or have DBZ style scouters!</div> </div> </div> </div>What you want to refute it's a direct quote from M20. Also you really should read my post...because I literally said that. Like, literally.<br /> <br /> And as for the rest, Spheres don't matter if you, the Player, don't know how to use your Instruments in a thematic way. Magely bullshit it's a beautifull art, I would rather accept that I can't cast a spell &quot;because my Paradigm&quot; rather than casting it in in a way that fails to, at least, convince or appeal to myself. That's what I understand as &quot;sincerity&quot;. Imagination and knowledge makes this endeavor a lot easier, of course. You won't apply aerospace engineering to fix a broken leg and I wouldn't apply a kung-fu punch to change sex, nobody said that other Instruments can't cover it if it's within the more broad scope of the Paradigm. But maybe they can't, Imagination it's a fickle thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T15:52:32-07:00","id":1296536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1295835#post1295835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those limitations you mention apply only to those that believe in such limitations, and they're more a question of fluff than rules.<br /> <br /> 1\u00ba<br /> <br /> The first example you gave isn't nearly as limiting as you make it to be:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Although she couldn\u2019t fly through the air or skip along tree branches by manipulating chi (\u201cThat\u2019s just mythology!\u201d), she can still rework conventional physics and biology through her understanding of the fighting arts.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So I can't use Chi but I can &amp;quot;<i>rework conventional physics and biology through my understanding of the fighting arts&amp;quot;</i>?<br /> <br /> OK: I rework gravity to nulify my weight and reverse asceleration <i>in order to fly trough the air and/or skip trough branches</i>. How it's that beyond &amp;quot;reworking conventional physics&amp;quot;...which apparently I can do with &amp;quot;my figthing arts&amp;quot;? There's very few things I can't do if I can &amp;quot;rework conventional physics and biology&amp;quot; with kung-fu...<br /> <br /> In other words:<br /> <br /> You're reading that paragraph like it's limiting what Science! can do, but in truth it's merely pointing out that Science! uses a different explanation to do exactly the same things<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that Scientific Mystics can believe in Chi, they will just think it's ancient science.<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba<br /> <br /> The sidebar it's confusing, I grant you that (and contradicts itself when it says that technomancers can't do certain things...then proceding to give rules to do literal &amp;quot;handwavium&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I don't like that sidebar, but it's understandable if you remember how Focus it's now divided in three parts.<br /> <br /> ALL mages have to explain how their magick works: While magick it's a very convinient explanation sometimes <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MagicAIsMagicA&amp;quot;]Magic</a> A is Magic A[/URL] and if a Chi user can't really explain how their approach to Chi and wuxia transforms them into a dog in a convincing way they can't do it...with that Instrument, but they may be able to do so if they have surpassed that Instrument or just decide to use the rules to cast w/o Instrument to work on Paradigm alone (If Reality is an Ilussion maybe I can be a dog...). Since Technomancers don't get to cast this way so easily M20 has a sidebar providing an alternative way (casting with a weird explanation).<br /> <br /> If you read that sidebar again you will notice that the explanation has to &amp;quot;make sense&amp;quot; to the technomancer...it doesn't have to &amp;quot;be true&amp;quot; nor to be reasonable from the pov of conventional science. It's a very light limitation that borders on none at all. It has even been debated than thanks to that sidebar M20 technomagick may be less limiting than mystic magick because mystics don't get to use &amp;quot;handwavium&amp;quot; when thay can't explain what they're doing...if this balances out with magick being a convinient explanation or not depends, really, on the imagination, knowledge (and sincerity) of the player...For instance, I don't think most Chi users turn into litaral animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 has several entries stating that technomancers/technocrats cannot cast or use several mystic instruments or even wonders because they don't believe in magick. I don't think that you can simply throw quantum shit or any scientific term into the effect explanation and it's done.<br /> There is no way a Scientist would believe that it's possible to turn into a dog, or fly, using meditation and body energy. I would accept using a machine. <br /> Nowadays we are too dependent of machinery to do things, we just don't believe in body energy so much.<br /> <br /> M20 pg529:<br /> <br /> &quot;The second part is a bit trickier: Does your mage BELIEVE that he can do such things? Sure, maybe you\u2019ve got Forces 3 and Prime 2 on your character sheet. A Black Suit can\u2019t just snap her fingers and make fireballs appear, however. Such feats don\u2019t fit her focus \u2013 they violate her beliefs. She can\u2019t conjure fire using someone else\u2019s focus, either; if you gave her a rune-carved staff, she\u2019d try to hit someone with it, not summon a firestorm. That sort of nonsense is Reality Deviance, and so \u2013 Spheres be damned \u2013 the Black Suit could no more conjure fire with a staff than she could fart unicorns and shoot them into space.&quot;<br /> <br /> This leads to the issue. Considering we all agree that those explanations are just crap, would the technomancer not be able to cast, or just cast as vulgar magick?<br /> The book makes us believe that everything that is considered magic, like flying in a broom stick, can't be done by Scientists. And i bet he also couldn't just think that the broom is &quot;distorting gravity by shifting etc...&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, I think there is a big difference between magick and technomagic. A mage could explain his effect a lot easier with &quot;it's magick&quot; or &quot;God did it&quot;, while the technomancer should have a good scientific explanation for it to work, otherwise he would be just a mage. If he believes that he can turn into a dog by self-hypnosis or placebo effect he might be a mage.<br /> <br /> Also, i think that technomancers can use psionics or martial arts, but they couldn't use them for more than what is acceptable by today's science, like healing, improving attributes, even telekinesis (vulgar) or pirokinesis (also vulgar). But no flying, turning into dog, turning into fire, opening a portal to the umbra. Those crazy effects would require him to be a mystic, or use some kind of machine.<br /> <br /> Am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T20:40:12-07:00","id":1296584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296536#post1296536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 has several entries stating that technomancers/technocrats cannot cast or use several mystic instruments or even wonders because they don't believe in magick. I don't think that you can simply throw quantum shit or any scientific term into the effect explanation and it's done.<br /> There is no way a Scientist would believe that it's possible to turn into a dog, or fly, using meditation and body energy. I would accept using a machine.<br /> Nowadays we are too dependent of machinery to do things, we just don't believe in body energy so much.<br /> <br /> M20 pg529:<br /> <br /> &quot;The second part is a bit trickier: Does your mage BELIEVE that he can do such things? Sure, maybe you\u2019ve got Forces 3 and Prime 2 on your character sheet. A Black Suit can\u2019t just snap her fingers and make fireballs appear, however. Such feats don\u2019t fit her focus \u2013 they violate her beliefs. She can\u2019t conjure fire using someone else\u2019s focus, either; if you gave her a rune-carved staff, she\u2019d try to hit someone with it, not summon a firestorm. That sort of nonsense is Reality Deviance, and so \u2013 Spheres be damned \u2013 the Black Suit could no more conjure fire with a staff than she could fart unicorns and shoot them into space.&quot;<br /> <br /> This leads to the issue. Considering we all agree that those explanations are just crap, would the technomancer not be able to cast, or just cast as vulgar magick?<br /> The book makes us believe that everything that is considered magic, like flying in a broom stick, can't be done by Scientists. And i bet he also couldn't just think that the broom is &quot;distorting gravity by shifting etc...&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, I think there is a big difference between magick and technomagic. A mage could explain his effect a lot easier with &quot;it's magick&quot; or &quot;God did it&quot;, while the technomancer should have a good scientific explanation for it to work, otherwise he would be just a mage. If he believes that he can turn into a dog by self-hypnosis or placebo effect he might be a mage.<br /> <br /> Also, i think that technomancers can use psionics or martial arts, but they couldn't use them for more than what is acceptable by today's science, like healing, improving attributes, even telekinesis (vulgar) or pirokinesis (also vulgar). But no flying, turning into dog, turning into fire, opening a portal to the umbra. Those crazy effects would require him to be a mystic, or use some kind of machine.<br /> <br /> Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, the biggest difference is that some people want to put Technomancers in a special box they don't want to put normal Magick in because they haven't done any study on the subject. Waving your fingers and turning someone into a dog is no more a part of Hermetic theory or even &quot;A god just did it I don't have to explain&quot; for Chorusters.. Every Faction has a structure equally in Depth and JUST AS constraining or not at Science. IF you can't think of a Technomancer that can turn someone into a Dog.. Don't Buy Life four.<br /> <br /> M20 book of secrets<br /> <br /> Scientific Mystic /Techgnosi (3 pt. Merit)<br /> Certain unorthodox technomancers understand that<br /> \u201cmysticism\u201d is just another form of science whose principles<br /> may be understood by a properly Enlightened mind. Although<br /> you pursue a technological practice and employ tech-based<br /> instruments, you can employ instruments that are traditionally<br /> considered to be \u201cmagic\u201d once you\u2019ve had an opportunity to<br /> study them and fit those tools into your scientific paradigm.<br /> The Scientific Mystic Merit lets a dedicated technomancer<br /> \u2013 that is, a member of the Society of Ether, the Virtual Adepts,<br /> a tech-based \u201corphan,\u201d or perhaps even a rogue Technocrat<br /> like the Disparates of Navalon \u2013 study metaphysical principles<br /> from mystic-paradigm mages for no extra point-cost if<br /> that technomancer has the focus practice Weird Science.<br /> (For details, see Can a Mage Who Uses One Type of Focus<br /> Learn Magick from a Mage Who Uses a Different Kind of<br /> Focus?, Chapter Three, p. 174, and the Weird Science entry in<br /> Mage 20, p. 584.) That technomancer can also choose traditionally<br /> \u201cmystic\u201d tools as up to half of her required instruments<br /> (as detailed under Arete, Focus, and Instruments in Mage 20,<br /> p. 329), and can discard those instruments as a mystic instead<br /> of as a technomancer (again, see Mage 20, p. 329). Essentially,<br /> this means that your approach to Enlightened science is flexible<br /> enough to embrace bizarre approaches to your metaphysical<br /> pursuits. Other scientists might consider such things impossible,<br /> but you realize that \u201cpossibility\u201d is what you make of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:53:04-07:00","id":1296651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296536#post1296536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 has several entries stating that technomancers/technocrats cannot cast or use several mystic instruments or even wonders because they don't believe in magick. I don't think that you can simply throw quantum shit or any scientific term into the effect explanation and it's done.<br /> There is no way a Scientist would believe that it's possible to turn into a dog, or fly, using meditation and body energy. I would accept using a machine.<br /> Nowadays we are too dependent of machinery to do things, we just don't believe in body energy so much.<br /> <br /> M20 pg529:<br /> <br /> &quot;The second part is a bit trickier: Does your mage BELIEVE that he can do such things? Sure, maybe you\u2019ve got Forces 3 and Prime 2 on your character sheet. A Black Suit can\u2019t just snap her fingers and make fireballs appear, however. Such feats don\u2019t fit her focus \u2013 they violate her beliefs. She can\u2019t conjure fire using someone else\u2019s focus, either; if you gave her a rune-carved staff, she\u2019d try to hit someone with it, not summon a firestorm. That sort of nonsense is Reality Deviance, and so \u2013 Spheres be damned \u2013 the Black Suit could no more conjure fire with a staff than she could fart unicorns and shoot them into space.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor but very important distinction here. The Black Suit is not a technomancer. The Black Suit is a Technocrat. There is a significant different between the two. Technocrats have a serious issue getting away from using science, to the point that they can't even surpass foci. Technomancers can do stuff like breathe Ether and try to refine raw sunlight from oranges. Technocrats, even Void Engineers explicitly cannot do these things.<br /> <br /> The only thing we really know about Technomancers is that they have a hard, but not impossible, time surpassing their instruments. I would argue this means they don't even have to be particularly scientific, their paradigm just has to be extrinsic. Even if you want to limit it to science, though, it would still include Mages who follow a natural philosophy paradigm out of the 1600s, Mages who take a Victorian spiritualist approach to science, and Mages who make Star Trek technobabble sound reasonable (and Star Trek had someone turn into a newt because they went past Warp 10. I am not making that up.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This leads to the issue. Considering we all agree that those explanations are just crap, would the technomancer not be able to cast, or just cast as vulgar magick?<br /> The book makes us believe that everything that is considered magic, like flying in a broom stick, can't be done by Scientists. And i bet he also couldn't just think that the broom is &quot;distorting gravity by shifting etc...&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The Mage's belief determines whether they are able to cast. The consensus determines if local reality accepts it or not. There is some speculation that the Mage's beliefs do affect the Vulgarity, and you can use that if you think there is good reason. Personally, I'd argue it is mostly there as an example of the kind of debates Mages get up to.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T06:44:00-07:00","id":1296678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296584#post1296584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, the biggest difference is that some people want to put Technomancers in a special box they don't want to put normal Magick in because they haven't done any study on the subject. Waving your fingers and turning someone into a dog is no more a part of Hermetic theory or even &amp;quot;A god just did it I don't have to explain&amp;quot; for Chorusters.. Every Faction has a structure equally in Depth and JUST AS constraining or not at Science. IF you can't think of a Technomancer that can turn someone into a Dog.. Don't Buy Life four.<br /> <br /> M20 book of secrets<br /> <br /> Scientific Mystic /Techgnosi (3 pt. Merit)<br /> Certain unorthodox technomancers understand that<br /> \u201cmysticism\u201d is just another form of science whose principles<br /> may be understood by a properly Enlightened mind. Although<br /> you pursue a technological practice and employ tech-based<br /> instruments, you can employ instruments that are traditionally<br /> considered to be \u201cmagic\u201d once you\u2019ve had an opportunity to<br /> study them and fit those tools into your scientific paradigm.<br /> The Scientific Mystic Merit lets a dedicated technomancer<br /> \u2013 that is, a member of the Society of Ether, the Virtual Adepts,<br /> a tech-based \u201corphan,\u201d or perhaps even a rogue Technocrat<br /> like the Disparates of Navalon \u2013 study metaphysical principles<br /> from mystic-paradigm mages for no extra point-cost if<br /> that technomancer has the focus practice Weird Science.<br /> (For details, see Can a Mage Who Uses One Type of Focus<br /> Learn Magick from a Mage Who Uses a Different Kind of<br /> Focus?, Chapter Three, p. 174, and the Weird Science entry in<br /> Mage 20, p. 584.) That technomancer can also choose traditionally<br /> \u201cmystic\u201d tools as up to half of her required instruments<br /> (as detailed under Arete, Focus, and Instruments in Mage 20,<br /> p. 329), and can discard those instruments as a mystic instead<br /> of as a technomancer (again, see Mage 20, p. 329). Essentially,<br /> this means that your approach to Enlightened science is flexible<br /> enough to embrace bizarre approaches to your metaphysical<br /> pursuits. Other scientists might consider such things impossible,<br /> but you realize that \u201cpossibility\u201d is what you make of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just proves my point. They even have to take a merit to be able to do what you guys are saying. <br /> And the mystic also have to explain his effect, i never said otherwise. But it is a lot easier to explain when you don't have to base in scientific reality and can use spirits and energies to explain it. This way you can explain turning yourself into fire with meditation, while a technomancer can't. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that a technomancer can't turn himself into fire, just that he couldn't using meditation. Maybe some special chamber..<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> I think you're right. There is a difference between technocrats and technomancers. Even so, as you said, the mage must believe in what he's doing to be able to do it. And no scientist would believe in any explanationbto turn himself into a dog or fire just by meditating. Or if he does believes, his peers won't and he would be laughed at in his tradition. Probably changing to a mystic tradition that would accept his magick the way he believes.<br /> <br /> I think it would be easier for the scientist to join a mystic tradition like Akashic, hermetic or chorus and approach his focus by a scientific view than to be in a technomancer tradition, using mystic like ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T07:50:35-07:00","id":1296694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296678#post1296678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just proves my point. They even have to take a merit to be able to do what you guys are saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they have to take a Merit to use mystical theory and Instruments (to explain what they do as Chi, like I said) , and to be able to discard half of them like a Mystic. That paragraph <b>in no way</b> proves that <u><i>Mad Science</i></u> <i>has to be</i> <i>reasonable </i>to scientists - that would be crazy. Mad science it's <i>supposed </i>to be bullshit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the mystic also have to explain his effect, i never said otherwise. But it is a lot easier to explain when you don't have to base in scientific reality and can use spirits and energies to explain it. This way you can explain turning yourself into fire with meditation, while a technomancer can't.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that a technomancer can't turn himself into fire, just that he couldn't using meditation. Maybe some special chamber.. </div> </div> </div>One of the characters from the Etherite Tradition Book uses psychic powers as his focus (and why not?, psionics it's a very traditional pseudoscience). Even Technocrats sometimes dabble on it. This also happens to be a Practice in M20 that technomancers can take w/o the Merit.<br /> <br /> Now, if you know anything about psychic powers, it includes things like telekinesis and pyrokinesis. In WoD these are considered to be Static magic in spite of being deep on the pseudoscience/bullshit scale . Awakened psionics have every right to be more flexible with their power. Hence, since &quot;Mind over body&quot; it's part of that Practice and also Pyrokinesis, I would allow the Etherite Psion to combine these approaches and turn into fire with meditation. Of course, this is not because &quot;reality is an illusion&quot; but merely tapping on the untold potential of human mind (which apparently includes things like summoning fire from nowhere, ignoring every physical law - really, I don't see why transformation of the self would be much crazier than that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even so, as you said, the mage must believe in what he's doing to be able to do it. And no scientist would believe in any explanationbto turn himself into a dog or fire just by meditating. Or if he does believes, his peers won't and he would be laughed at in his tradition. Probably changing to a mystic tradition that would accept his magick the way he believes.<br /> <br /> I think it would be easier for the scientist to join a mystic tradition like Akashic, hermetic or chorus and approach his focus by a scientific view than to be in a technomancer tradition, using mystic like ways. </div> </div> </div>Since some of the greatest Etherites (doc Eon) are recognized Scientific Mystics, I think your wrong (Besides, what kind of Etherite, nay, what kind of <i>Mad Scientist</i>, would accept to be regarded as a &quot;wizard&quot; becuase he was laughed at- They laughed at me, They said That I was Mad! But Who Is Mad Now!?. No other faction supports this playstile like the Etherites, it's their thing)<br /> <br /> I'm not onboard with your reasonable aproach to Mad Science - and ultimately it's not supported by the books, as shown by the fact that every quote you posted talks about Technocrats (who aren't too fond of Mad Scientists, albeit they do have a few among their ranks)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-14-2019, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T08:09:43-07:00","id":1296698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296678#post1296678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> I think you're right. There is a difference between technocrats and technomancers. Even so, as you said, the mage must believe in what he's doing to be able to do it. And no scientist would believe in any explanation to turn himself into a dog or fire just by meditating. Or if he does believes, his peers won't and he would be laughed at in his tradition. Probably changing to a mystic tradition that would accept his magick the way he believes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there was ever a Tradition for someone who would say, &quot;They laughed! Can you believe it? They laughed at me! Well I'll show them! I'll show them all!!! Mwa ha ha ha!&quot; it would be the Etherites <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: It is very telling that both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> and I reached for the &quot;They laughed at me!&quot; trope to describe the SoE.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, there is a difference between the beliefs that make someone a Technomancer and what beliefs a Tradition will accept. Someone could have a completely unscientific approach to their magic (say, &quot;there is an angel for every effect, every angel has a true name, writing their name exactly correctly will make them show up and do their effect&quot;) and if it is still an extrinsic approach they would be a Technomancer. That doesn't mean they'd find understanding in the Etherites or the Virtual Adepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it would be easier for the scientist to join a mystic tradition like Akashic, hermetic or chorus and approach his focus by a scientific view than to be in a technomancer tradition, using mystic like ways. </div> </div> </div>I think you are underestimating how big a change that is. The Akashics, for instance, see the forms and practice of martial arts and meditation as a path to Enlightenment and understanding. As far as they are concerned the motions and thoughts themselves don't do anything, they are just a guide that can be dropped once you don't need them. They would say that studying why meditation lets you turn into a dog entirely misses the point. &quot;Meditation doesn't let you turn into a dog. Understanding that you are a dog is what makes you a dog. Please put down the electrodes.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Etherites might laugh at theories that let someone meditate their way to doghood, but they'd at least recognize the spirit and reason for scientific inquiry. Despite the general tone of mockery, they are still the best fit.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, I mean that specifically for the Technomancer. Your previous character, since he thinks of himself as part of the effect, would not be a Technomancer. His approach is a closer fit for the Hermetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-14-2019, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T17:57:00-07:00","id":1296844,"title":"","content":"Ok, I am convinced. Indeed, most of the quotes I had in mind were about technocrats nd not technomancers, altough some of them (the ones found in the practices Yoga and Martial Arts description) did mention technomancers.<br /> But the point seems to be: your char can cast what he believes that he can do. This is clear now. And the tradition/convention he belongs can or cannot influence into his practices deppending on which is it. A technocrat that believes he can turn into fire by meditating might be dealt with right away, while a etherite would be laughed at and a hermetic would be praised.<br /> <br /> And, according to Science!, if an effect has too many bullshit science explanation it goes vulgar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296698#post1296698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all seriousness, there is a difference between the beliefs that make someone a Technomancer and what beliefs a Tradition will accept. Someone could have a completely unscientific approach to their magic (say, &quot;there is an angel for every effect, every angel has a true name, writing their name exactly correctly will make them show up and do their effect&quot;) and if it is still an extrinsic approach they would be a Technomancer. That doesn't mean they'd find understanding in the Etherites or the Virtual Adepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you meant with that I don't get it.<br /> <br /> And yes, I still think that my char would fit better as hermetic, but I find it curious that just the addition of the Will (since my hermetic also have a scientific view of things) in the equation makes him a mystic and the etherite is still a technomancer.<br /> <br /> Also, I want to use this thread to think a bit more how would be an hermetic that doesn't use High Ritual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T05:34:55-07:00","id":1296956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296844#post1296844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, according to Science!, if an effect has too many bullshit science explanation it goes vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be careful with this one. The standard rules for Vulgarity still apply. A device that subtly alters the probabilities of bullet trajectories is probably coincidental whether it is powered by demons (Hermetic), Quantum Probability (Technocracy), or energy that the inventor literally named &quot;Etheric Bullshit&quot; (particularly zany Etherites). Instead, I think this section is referencing those times when scientific looking explanations offer good cover to make things coincidental. A ritual circle does nothing to make directing lightning look like it is possible, a doodad with a radar dish and a large antenna might. However a bunch of donkeys on treadmills powering a gigantic lightbulb is not going to convince any bystanders that the inventor can direct lightning, no matter how much she insists that the principles are sound.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you meant with that I don't get it.<br /> <br /> And yes, I still think that my char would fit better as hermetic, but I find it curious that just the addition of the Will (since my hermetic also have a scientific view of things) in the equation makes him a mystic and the etherite is still a technomancer. </div> </div> </div>This goes back to the Intrinsic vs Extrinsic distinction we were talking about earlier<br /> <br /> The main thing we know about Technomancers is that they have a harder time giving up Foci/Practices than mystics, but not as difficult a time as full Technomancers. This seems to be primarily because they do not believe that they can do anything without their tools (whether those tools are physical gadgets or mental patterns). Their paradigms are extrinsic. Now because the only two examples of Technomancers we have are the Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts it is easy to think that the issue is with the scientific approach. However, one of the elements of Mage is that everyone is doing the same thing, no paradigm is inherently privileged. So any approach that puts all of the power in the tools and none of it in the tool user should have the same problem giving up foci/practices, even if it is not remotely scientific.<br /> <br /> The Angel Namer I proposed earlier would be an example. She believes that it is the carving of an angel's name that summons them, that anyone can do this if they know how to carve the names just right, and that the angels do not think or respond to commands they just appear and do whatever task they always do. She clearly has nothing to do with technology but she is not part of the magic at all, so she should have the same issues surpassing foci. <br /> <br /> For the same reason a scientific paradigm that drops the focus on tools and taps into the 'scientist's' own Understanding, or Will, Genius would become intrinsic. Even though it still has the same look as any other scientific paradigm it would still incorporate the scientist himself as an irreplaceable part of the system. Your hermetic is an example of this. He is researching his powers and detailing the laws that govern them, but he is also aware that the average person on the street cannot do what he does even if they had access to all his notes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I want to use this thread to think a bit more how would be an hermetic that doesn't use High Ritual... </div> </div> </div>What did you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:28:24-07:00","id":1296978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296956#post1296956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be careful with this one. The standard rules for Vulgarity still apply. A device that subtly alters the probabilities of bullet trajectories is probably coincidental whether it is powered by demons (Hermetic), Quantum Probability (Technocracy), or energy that the inventor literally named &amp;quot;Etheric Bullshit&amp;quot; (particularly zany Etherites). Instead, I think this section is referencing those times when scientific looking explanations offer good cover to make things coincidental. A ritual circle does nothing to make directing lightning look like it is possible, a doodad with a radar dish and a large antenna might. However a bunch of donkeys on treadmills powering a gigantic lightbulb is not going to convince any bystanders that the inventor can direct lightning, no matter how much she insists that the principles are sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. Tje sidebar refers for vulgar effects that can be made coincident by explaining with science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296956#post1296956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes back to the Intrinsic vs Extrinsic distinction we were talking about earlier<br /> <br /> The main thing we know about Technomancers is that they have a harder time giving up Foci/Practices than mystics, but not as difficult a time as full Technomancers. This seems to be primarily because they do not believe that they can do anything without their tools (whether those tools are physical gadgets or mental patterns). Their paradigms are extrinsic. Now because the only two examples of Technomancers we have are the Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts it is easy to think that the issue is with the scientific approach. However, one of the elements of Mage is that everyone is doing the same thing, no paradigm is inherently privileged. So any approach that puts all of the power in the tools and none of it in the tool user should have the same problem giving up foci/practices, even if it is not remotely scientific.<br /> <br /> The Angel Namer I proposed earlier would be an example. She believes that it is the carving of an angel's name that summons them, that anyone can do this if they know how to carve the names just right, and that the angels do not think or respond to commands they just appear and do whatever task they always do. She clearly has nothing to do with technology but she is not part of the magic at all, so she should have the same issues surpassing foci. <br /> <br /> For the same reason a scientific paradigm that drops the focus on tools and taps into the 'scientist's' own Understanding, or Will, Genius would become intrinsic. Even though it still has the same look as any other scientific paradigm it would still incorporate the scientist himself as an irreplaceable part of the system. Your hermetic is an example of this. He is researching his powers and detailing the laws that govern them, but he is also aware that the average person on the street cannot do what he does even if they had access to all his notes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes perfect sense. Unfortunately, the books classify mystic and technomancers by their tradition and not how they view their focus. Do you have any quote from M20 that explains what you just posted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296956#post1296956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, reading the hermetic tradition book section about recruitment and training, i don't know if my char would fit 100%. In their training they learn goetia and theurgy that are some kind of static magic and they go through language learning (he won't have any dot in language). Also, it seems that in this process they learn high ritual magic and at least for now I'm not planning in adding this practice to the char (unless i can adapt it into his style, he's not going to use any material component). <br /> <br /> So, I was wondering if there could be an hermetic that doesn't use high ritual magic and how he would be seen in the order","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:28:35-07:00","id":1296979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now because the only two examples of Technomancers we have are the Sons of Ether and the Virtual Adepts it is easy to think that the issue is with the scientific approach. However, one of the elements of Mage is that everyone is doing the same thing, no paradigm is inherently privileged. So any approach that puts all of the power in the tools and none of it in the tool user should have the same problem giving up foci/practices, even if it is not remotely scientific.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I think things should be. But sadly books offer very little to justify this approach, with a language that clearly relates technomagick and science, and a clasification that divides these by Faction. Ironically, it's older books where we can find esoterical &quot;technomancers&quot; (Childern of Knowledge were depicted as such, and also Taftani)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the same reason a scientific paradigm that drops the focus on tools and taps into the 'scientist's' own Understanding, or Will, Genius would become intrinsic. </div> </div> </div>A very good example of this would be those who practice Psionics. Students of pshychic phenomena always stress that the power comes from your mind/self and things like meditation and cristals are, literally, focuses. But again, books aren't very supportive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-15-2019, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:45:51-07:00","id":1296987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296978#post1296978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, reading the hermetic tradition book section about recruitment and training, i don't know if my char would fit 100%. In their training they learn goetia and theurgy that are some kind of static magic and they go through language learning (he won't have any dot in language). Also, it seems that in this process they learn high ritual magic and at least for now I'm not planning in adding this practice to the char (unless i can adapt it into his style, he's not going to use any material component).<br /> <br /> So, I was wondering if there could be an hermetic that doesn't use high ritual magic and how he would be seen in the order</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that not all recruits are taken trough the learning process. Only about half Hermetics Awaken in the Tradition, they don't have the numbers to reject similar minded mages just because they didn't go trough all the steps. Your mage would be one of these &quot;late&quot; recruits.<br /> <br /> Albeit High Ritual does not need material components (see the Instruments) I do se a problem if you don't want to employ the esoterical trappings of the Tradition in your Paradigm. It doesn't mean you can't be &quot;Hermetic&quot;, but you will be an outlier. That alone would put you squarely on Ex-Miscelanea regardless of your personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T08:46:01-07:00","id":1296999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296978#post1296978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes perfect sense. Unfortunately, the books classify mystic and technomancers by their tradition and not how they view their focus. Do you have any quote from M20 that explains what you just posted?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1296979#post1296979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how I think things should be. But sadly books offer very little to justify this approach, with a language that clearly relates technomagick and science, and a clasification that divides these by Faction. Ironically, it's older books where we can find esoterical &quot;technomancers&quot; (Childern of Knowledge were depicted as such, and also Taftani)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not from M20, no. As Aleph points out it isn't spelled out directly. Instead, there are indications in earlier books that other factions can have the same problem. Also of the two potential divides between mystic and technomancer, the Intrinsic/Extrinsic explanation fits considerably better with Mage's subjective approach than magic vs science. So while I wouldn't say that this is explicit in the book, it is the natural extension of things which are.<br /> <br /> That said, if you have reason to use the magic vs science explanation then go for it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, reading the hermetic tradition book section about recruitment and training, i don't know if my char would fit 100%. In their training they learn goetia and theurgy that are some kind of static magic and they go through language learning (he won't have any dot in language). Also, it seems that in this process they learn high ritual magic and at least for now I'm not planning in adding this practice to the char (unless i can adapt it into his style, he's not going to use any material component).<br /> <br /> So, I was wondering if there could be an hermetic that doesn't use high ritual magic and how he would be seen in the order </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Remember the Traditions stand ready to adopt most possible expressions of magic. Even if someone isn't a great fit for a Tradition or House, they may still find a place there if they match in other ways. Remember also that the Hermetics have picked up a lot of magical knowledge and styles over the years. If your mage matches House Flambeau in temperament and outlook, they could easily welcome him in even if they don't quite understand what he is up to. It certainly wouldn't be the first time.<br /> <br /> There is another option which might work for you. Your mage might officially be part of House Ex Miscellania but be attached to House Flambeau as some sort of representative or cross-house endeavor. That would put you in the proximity of mages who understand his style and mages who understand his personality. It would also offer quite a few story hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T18:09:59-07:00","id":1297117,"title":"","content":"Put him in house ex miscelania is not an option for me. I see him as an hermetic Flambeau, Tytalus or Bonisagus (in this order) or at max an etherite, even though I prefer hermetic.<br /> <br /> Now, he will be using as instruments mainly gestures and energy, but also meditation, eye contact, vocalization, exertion and weapons. Also he might use a talisman that's like a bracelet as focus too. Besides the talisman and weapons he won't be using any material component for his spells. For practices he uses psionics and martial arts. Don't know if chaos magick is a good choice too.<br /> <br /> If it's possible to adapt high ritual into his style it would be nice. He would cast spells in the style of dr. Strange or D&amp;D wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T18:58:14-07:00","id":1297123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297117#post1297117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put him in house ex miscelania is not an option for me. I see him as an hermetic Flambeau, Tytalus or Bonisagus (in this order) or at max an etherite, even though I prefer hermetic.<br /> <br /> Now, he will be using as instruments mainly gestures and energy, but also meditation, eye contact, vocalization, exertion and weapons. Also he might use a talisman that's like a bracelet as focus too. Besides the talisman and weapons he won't be using any material component for his spells. For practices he uses psionics and martial arts. Don't know if chaos magick is a good choice too.<br /> <br /> If it's possible to adapt high ritual into his style it would be nice. He would cast spells in the style of dr. Strange or D&amp;D wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hermetics are HIGH Magick. Where as an Etherite might take a part Magickal practices and find a &quot;Rational&quot; explanation. the Hermetic Takes apart science and finds a magical explanation(and to the extreme there is a FlIP side of Technomystic for Mystic practioners who want to incorporate scientific aspects into their paradigm... <br /> <br /> <br /> to quote m20: Alchemy, dominion, and High Ritual form core practices within the Order\u2019s ranks.<br /> No Hermetic mage lacks such training.<br /> <br /> You might throw in your wierd add ons.. but the assumption as a Hermetic is you're going to accept the foundation of Hermetic mysticism. IF high Ritual is not his Core then... he's not a Hermetic. This is the problem with the &quot;Magic is ANYTHING that's not Science' Theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T08:20:07-07:00","id":1297513,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't know if we should take these 2 lines so seriously. Afterall the books are always contradicting themselves and there aee exceptions.<br /> <br /> In the tradition book they don't focus so much in high ritual. In the paradigm and belief section, it states that the essence of the hermetic is the ascendancy of the Will. <br /> <br /> But, considering that high ritual is indeed needed, there are two options for this mage.<br /> <br /> 1: He was taught high ritual, but also martial arts and psionics and he just uses the last two<br /> <br /> 2: I can try to adapt high ritualbin conjunction with martial arts and psionics and all the instruments I posted before. Afterall, a mage's practice is almost unique and can be a mixture of several practices.<br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer option 2. As I said, i can see him doing gestures and vocalization in the style as dr Strange movie or a D&amp;D wizard (like a mage from Baldur's Gate or Neverwinter Nights PC games)<br /> I'm just not sure if these examples I gave indeed fit high ritual magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T21:42:00-07:00","id":1297639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297513#post1297513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't know if we should take these 2 lines so seriously. Afterall the books are always contradicting themselves and there aee exceptions.<br /> <br /> In the tradition book they don't focus so much in high ritual. In the paradigm and belief section, it states that the essence of the hermetic is the ascendancy of the Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also have a whole complicated series of intiations. Doctor strange is very much a person who uses High Ritual and Martial arts. He's also a guy who studied science and well.. rejected it. He may include a scientific view of many causes and effects, but that's probably true of most western mages, he just includes new ones on top of that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, considering that high ritual is indeed needed, there are two options for this mage.<br /> <br /> 1: He was taught high ritual, but also martial arts and psionics and he just uses the last two<br /> <br /> 2: I can try to adapt high ritualbin conjunction with martial arts and psionics and all the instruments I posted before. Afterall, a mage's practice is almost unique and can be a mixture of several practices.<br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer option 2. As I said, i can see him doing gestures and vocalization in the style as dr Strange movie or a D&amp;D wizard (like a mage from Baldur's Gate or Neverwinter Nights PC games)<br /> I'm just not sure if these examples I gave indeed fit high ritual magick. </div> </div> </div>Why do you want to include Psionics? Honestly meditation, martial arts, and high ritual seems to get the visuals you want. Hand gestures invoking powers.. the Psionics just seems kind of like an appendix to say he was a &quot;technomancer&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T07:37:01-07:00","id":1297717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can try to adapt high ritualbin conjunction with martial arts and psionics and all the instruments I posted before. Afterall, a mage's practice is almost unique and can be a mixture of several practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think combining Martial Arts/Psionics with High Ritual it's very doable. Many martial traditions are shrouded in ritual and esoterism.<br /> <br /> When I think about a High Ritual Martial Artist the Anime <i>Naruto </i>comes to mind. They have a lot of martial arts magic, but Ninjutsu and Genjutsu are made trough quick hand gestures (and sometimes talismans, language and other props, but most of the time it's just the mudras)<br /> <br /> You can choose 3 Practices, so it's within the rule. The Focus could be sumarized as: There are *forces* in the cosmos that ordinary science doesn't contemplate but can be understood manipulated with altered states of the body and the mind - practicable within Etherites or Hermetics. In the case of Hermetic I would try to give this Ritual Martial Art an occidental vive to make him less of an outlier. Perhaps the forms are based on the zodiac or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T23:46:35-07:00","id":1297894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297639#post1297639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They also have a whole complicated series of intiations. Doctor strange is very much a person who uses High Ritual and Martial arts. He's also a guy who studied science and well.. rejected it. He may include a scientific view of many causes and effects, but that's probably true of most western mages, he just includes new ones on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dr. Strange never rejected science. He just understood that there are other forces and things going on in the universe that science did not covered yet. And why is Dr. Strange using High Ritual as well? Which parto of his casting could be considered High Ritual? <br /> I mean, the gestures seems pretty simple and looks like he uses more of his body energy and magician Will than the complicated gesture or vocalization. IN fact, Dr. Strange cast spells without any complicated instrument. If that's what High Ritual looks like, I cab definitely fit it in my character focus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297639#post1297639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you want to include Psionics? Honestly meditation, martial arts, and high ritual seems to get the visuals you want. Hand gestures invoking powers.. the Psionics just seems kind of like an appendix to say he was a &quot;technomancer&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm..How would Psionics make him a technomancer? I added it to make his focus more dependant of his mind, body and specially his Will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297717#post1297717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think combining Martial Arts/Psionics with High Ritual it's very doable. Many martial traditions are shrouded in ritual and esoterism.<br /> <br /> When I think about a High Ritual Martial Artist the Anime <i>Naruto </i>comes to mind. They have a lot of martial arts magic, but Ninjutsu and Genjutsu are made trough quick hand gestures (and sometimes talismans, language and other props, but most of the time it's just the mudras)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know and never seen naruto..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297717#post1297717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can choose 3 Practices, so it's within the rule. The Focus could be sumarized as: There are *forces* in the cosmos that ordinary science doesn't contemplate but can be understood manipulated with altered states of the body and the mind - practicable within Etherites or Hermetics. In the case of Hermetic I would try to give this Ritual Martial Art an occidental vive to make him less of an outlier. Perhaps the forms are based on the zodiac or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's pretty much what I want. Just need to see how the instruments are going to fit the high ritual part. I mean, what's the diference of using meditation, hand gesture, energy and vocalization with high ritual and with martial arts or psionics??<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T00:33:16-07:00","id":1297899,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, I am one of those folks that is rather dissatisfied with how technomancers are handled in the Mage ruleset;<br /> <br /> To me, technomancers are, essentially, just Mages that use modern tools instead of those of ye olde day. It's pretty much the only defining difference between a Technomancer and a non-Technomancer to me.<br /> It does not define wether the mage has a more scientific mindset, a mystic mindset, or anything in between - it's really just the flavor of their tool set, an organic evolution coming from Mages that simply got born in a different age.<br /> <br /> It does not define, per se, paradigm.<br /> And along those lines, I don't see why Technomancers should drop instruments later than the Mages that use tools of Ye Olde. *Both* kinds of Mages see their tools as just as important as the other at the start. There is no difference.<br /> <br /> The *real* difference, the one that changes the rules of tool dropping, should be purely Mystic vs. strictly Technocrat-Scientific enlightened mindsets. Mostly &lt;insert groups here&gt; vs. Technocracy, although I have no doubt there are unaffiliated Mages that have a Technocratic-Science mindset; It'd be silly to think that the Union would be the only ones to develop this, given that you also get unaffiliated mystics.<br /> <br /> <br /> In view of that, I think there should be no merit for a 'Technomancer to also use mystic tools' - to the Technomancer, their tools might *already* be mystical. They just happen to be of glass and metal, of electric power and intricate transistor patterns of arcane assembly, instead of wood and song. And *espeically* dual-Tradition trained Mages can easily already use both, the tools of olde and new, though that's not a requirement.<br /> <br /> No, I think the actual Merit should be one that specifically allows the Technocratic-scientific Mage to use Mystic tools - probably usually taken by those unaffiliated to the Union. I think there is actually such a merit - possibly, it's the same already mentioned, but I don't think it should be required for Technomancers in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-19-2019, 03:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T01:47:22-07:00","id":1297905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297894#post1297894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dr. Strange never rejected science. He just understood that there are other forces and things going on in the universe that science did not covered yet. And why is Dr. Strange using High Ritual as well? Which parto of his casting could be considered High Ritual?<br /> I mean, the gestures seems pretty simple and looks like he uses more of his body energy and magician Will than the complicated gesture or vocalization. IN fact, Dr. Strange cast spells without any complicated instrument. If that's what High Ritual looks like, I cab definitely fit it in my character focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Rejected might be too strong a word. He doesn't incorporate Science into his magic. His magic is.. magic. He might still understand medicine like most most modern western mages would still believe in germ theory but he doesn't make magical powered armor or mix up alchemical prescription drugs.<br /> <br /> High Ritual like Martial arts is a life style. Martial arts includes the time in a day he spends practicing and working out. Same is true with High Ritual. In the blink of combat he's probably making a couple of gestures and calling upon the right shiny ring or rubbing his necklace. But he's also spending the time to make and consecrate his magic rings at home during his &quot;down time&quot;. So its mostly simple gestures and invocations.. except when you need to spend 3 days building up Successes then its a more extended Ritual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hm..How would Psionics make him a technomancer? I added it to make his focus more dependant of his mind, body and specially his Will. </div> </div> </div>Because Psionics is a &quot;Science&quot; its a discredited one but it basically was/is an attempt to incorporate more blatant magical practices into a &quot;scientific&quot; explanation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, that's pretty much what I want. Just need to see how the instruments are going to fit the high ritual part. I mean, what's the diference of using meditation, hand gesture, energy and vocalization with high ritual and with martial arts or psionics?? </div> </div> </div>Visual Cues really. Doctor Strange is high ritual. Professor x is Psionics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T01:51:04-07:00","id":1297906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297899#post1297899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I think the actual Merit should be one that specifically allows the Technocratic-scientific Mage to use Mystic tools - probably usually taken by those unaffiliated to the Union. I think there is actually such a merit - possibly, it's the same already mentioned, but I don't think it should be required for Technomancers in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit Gives you twice the number of Instraments. Its functionally Dual Tradition without giving you sphere bonus and is costed about half for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T22:40:24-07:00","id":1298109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297905#post1297905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Rejected might be too strong a word. He doesn't incorporate Science into his magic. His magic is.. magic. He might still understand medicine like most most modern western mages would still believe in germ theory but he doesn't make magical powered armor or mix up alchemical prescription drugs.<br /> <br /> High Ritual like Martial arts is a life style. Martial arts includes the time in a day he spends practicing and working out. Same is true with High Ritual. In the blink of combat he's probably making a couple of gestures and calling upon the right shiny ring or rubbing his necklace. But he's also spending the time to make and consecrate his magic rings at home during his &quot;down time&quot;. So its mostly simple gestures and invocations.. except when you need to spend 3 days building up Successes then its a more extended Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nowhere writen that the mage must spend hour of his day doing something related to his practices. At best, they might spend some time doing it (meditating or practicing in the case of martial arts) because they like it, but that's not a rule.<br /> And Dr. Strange's ring and necklace are artifacts, they are not part of his focus, they are more like wonders.Also the assumption you made that he made (all his artefacts were already made) or consecrate them is wrong. If anything, Strange probably meditates or study his mystical arts, but surely not on a daily basis or any basis to let him cast so many spells like he does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297905#post1297905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Psionics is a &quot;Science&quot; its a discredited one but it basically was/is an attempt to incorporate more blatant magical practices into a &quot;scientific&quot; explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see. Yes, getting some kind of &quot;scientific&quot; explanation is something I also want in my char, that's why I think Psionics might work as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297905#post1297905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Visual Cues really. Doctor Strange is high ritual. Professor x is Psionics.</div> </div> </div> </div>They use completely different instruments. Professor X doesn't use gestures, he just needs to talk, actually not even that, he just needs to concentrate and use his mind powers.<br /> You are comparing two differents and classifying as practices. What I want to know is how is a hand gesture from a High Ritual different from a Martial art user. And why is Dr. Strange gesture considered High Ritual.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T05:26:12-07:00","id":1298124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1297894#post1297894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's pretty much what I want. Just need to see how the instruments are going to fit the high ritual part. I mean, what's the diference of using meditation, hand gesture, energy and vocalization with high ritual and with martial arts or psionics??</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a few differences in the skills that you use to aid the magic roll if you use that rule. I'd expect classic hermetic high ritual to focus around academics, lore, or perhaps a bit of theology. If there is more of a psionic/bioenergy focus, you might instead consider meditation, lore, or possibly medicine to be more prominent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T05:57:15-07:00","id":1298128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298109#post1298109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want to know is how is a hand gesture from a High Ritual different from a Martial art user. And why is Dr. Strange gesture considered High Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly meaning.<br /> <br /> A martial artist hand gesture channels the power of your body/mind - channeling Chi, for instance. A high ritual hand gesture channels cosmic power - channeling the power of an Angel, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T06:22:55-07:00","id":1298130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298109#post1298109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is nowhere writen that the mage must spend hour of his day doing something related to his practices. At best, they might spend some time doing it (meditating or practicing in the case of martial arts) because they like it, but that's not a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Entire premise of the game is that Magic is a life style. That its a clash of Cultures and whether or not a multicultural system can function vs a single monoculture that rises us all up out of squalor. This is explicitly spelled out in the Revised Hermetic book... but it pretty solidly the base of the game. They don't do it because they &quot;Like it&quot; they do it because it defines who they are as a person. Like people of Faith go to Church, people who find enlightnement in Martial arts.. practice Martial arts. People who find truth in high Ritual, live a ritualistic life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Dr. Strange's ring and necklace are artifacts, they are not part of his focus, they are more like wonders.Also the assumption you made that he made (all his artefacts were already made) or consecrate them is wrong. If anything, Strange probably meditates or study his mystical arts, but surely not on a daily basis or any basis to let him cast so many spells like he does. </div> </div> </div>A not insignficant number of his spells require particular items. While this could be covered by Wonders they could just as readily Unique Instraments. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh I see. Yes, getting some kind of &quot;scientific&quot; explanation is something I also want in my char, that's why I think Psionics might work as well. </div> </div> </div>Then you probably don't want to play a Hermetic. A Hermetic thinks Science is just another type of Magick. Psionics is saying magic is just another type of Science. They are direct inversions of each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They use completely different instruments. Professor X doesn't use gestures, he just needs to talk, actually not even that, he just needs to concentrate and use his mind powers.<br /> You are comparing two differents and classifying as practices. What I want to know is how is a hand gesture from a High Ritual different from a Martial art user. And why is Dr. Strange gesture considered High Ritual. </div> </div> </div>For someone who just &quot;Needs to talk&quot; Professor x does alot of &quot;putting his hand on his forhead&quot; to use psychic powers.. and or reaching out with his hands. I would arguing in MAGE terms that's when he's still using his instraments. When he just &quot;WILLS STUFF TO HAPPEN&quot; is him acting to surpass them.<br /> <br /> Finger Gestures do not a high Ritualist make, its about having a High Ritualist Life style. The finger gestures or calling upon the hoary Hosts are the in the moment &quot;quick&quot; rituals. He does INCLUDE Martial arts but compare him to heroes that are Martial arts Primary.. like say Iron Fist. There's a much more viceral up front quality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T07:01:19-07:00","id":1298135,"title":"","content":"It's true that a High Ritual mage it's going to have a High Ritual lifestile. This shouldn't be odd for someone that thinks <i>gods and other mystical forces are real and care about what you do</i>. Someone like that will most likely have odd behaviors to be on the good side of these occult forces.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean, however, that he needs to have trinkets to make rituals. There are lot's of trinketless rituals: fasting, praying every day, avoiding bad gestures at certain moments of the day and doing specific gestures at other moments, repeating mantras for hours, meditating on tought forms or keep potent Vows for weeks or months...these are all conducts you make to keep on the good graces of the cosmic powers and/or to manipulate them.<br /> <br /> Most real life Mystic Practices (martial or otherwise) DO include some kind of prop or trinket as part of their lifestile (martial astists keep lot's of oriental shit in their dojos, buddhists have lot's of ritual trinkets like altars or statues, chaos mages have altars made with stuff they recolect, students of pshychic phenomena surround themselves with cristals and good vive new agery stuff, and a big list of etc). The only real life Mystics I know that totally eschew trinkets are the hermit type of Tradition that actively try to avoid giving value to any material thing...<br /> <br /> ...but, of course, the value mystics give to their props <i>vary </i>and thus I can see a High Ritual mage that has no trinket as Instrument...this won't necessarily mean he won't dress funny or have tons of occult prop in his house, but rather than he merely puts more value on personal conduct than in material stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T10:01:57-07:00","id":1298163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298124#post1298124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably a few differences in the skills that you use to aid the magic roll if you use that rule. I'd expect classic hermetic high ritual to focus around academics, lore, or perhaps a bit of theology. If there is more of a psionic/bioenergy focus, you might instead consider meditation, lore, or possibly medicine to be more prominent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how academics, lore or theology has anything to do with meditation, hand gesture, energy and vocalization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Entire premise of the game is that Magic is a life style. That its a clash of Cultures and whether or not a multicultural system can function vs a single monoculture that rises us all up out of squalor. This is explicitly spelled out in the Revised Hermetic book... but it pretty solidly the base of the game. They don't do it because they &quot;Like it&quot; they do it because it defines who they are as a person. Like people of Faith go to Church, people who find enlightnement in Martial arts.. practice Martial arts. People who find truth in high Ritual, live a ritualistic life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the tradition book does have a sidebar about this, only to explain how could an hermetic use his slow casting High Ritual quickly in action situations. But how woul be a ritualistic life of a mage that combine the 3 practices (High Ritual, Martial arts and Psionics)?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking about changing Psionics for Chaos Magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A not insignficant number of his spells require particular items. While this could be covered by Wonders they could just as readily Unique Instraments.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in the movies, there is not a single spell I can remember that he uses any particular item. He relies only in hand gestures and energy to cast his spells. I still want to know why his style is considered High Ritual though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you probably don't want to play a Hermetic. A Hermetic thinks Science is just another type of Magick. Psionics is saying magic is just another type of Science. They are direct inversions of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>They know, as most mages too, that magick can be made with Science. But hermetics acknowledge and often study and respect science (low case). My character won't cast his spells using Science, he will just have a logical explanation for what he is doing. It's the internal/external focus thing. He knows that is his enlightened Will channeled through his focus that is doing the effect, and not just the result of using the instruments.<br /> The Psionics were added because it focus in the use of the mage's mind, body and Will to cast effects, which is what my char is going to use, that along with some logical explanation to what he's doing. I think it fits very well. But as I said, I might change for chaos magick, I don;t know..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For someone who just &quot;Needs to talk&quot; Professor x does alot of &quot;putting his hand on his forhead&quot; to use psychic powers.. and or reaching out with his hands. I would arguing in MAGE terms that's when he's still using his instraments. When he just &quot;WILLS STUFF TO HAPPEN&quot; is him acting to surpass them.<br /> <br /> Finger Gestures do not a high Ritualist make, its about having a High Ritualist Life style. The finger gestures or calling upon the hoary Hosts are the in the moment &quot;quick&quot; rituals. He does INCLUDE Martial arts but compare him to heroes that are Martial arts Primary.. like say Iron Fist. There's a much more viceral up front quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's why I added concentration. One might consider touching his forehead part of his instruments, maybe gestures, as well.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I didn't get what you meant in the second part of this quote.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true that a High Ritual mage it's going to have a High Ritual lifestile. This shouldn't be odd for someone that thinks <i>gods and other mystical forces are real and care about what you do</i>. Someone like that will most likely have odd behaviors to be on the good side of these occult forces.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean, however, that he needs to have trinkets to make rituals. There are lot's of trinketless rituals: fasting, praying every day, avoiding bad gestures at certain moments of the day and doing specific gestures at other moments, repeating mantras for hours, meditating on tought forms or keep potent Vows for weeks or months...these are all conducts you make to keep on the good graces of the cosmic powers and/or to manipulate them.<br /> <br /> Most real life Mystic Practices (martial or otherwise) DO include some kind of prop or trinket as part of their lifestile (martial astists keep lot's of oriental shit in their dojos, buddhists have lot's of ritual trinkets like altars or statues, chaos mages have altars made with stuff they recolect, students of pshychic phenomena surround themselves with cristals and good vive new agery stuff, and a big list of etc). The only real life Mystics I know that totally eschew trinkets are the hermit type of Tradition that actively try to avoid giving value to any material thing...<br /> <br /> ...but, of course, the value mystics give to their props <i>vary </i>and thus I can see a High Ritual mage that has no trinket as Instrument...this won't necessarily mean he won't dress funny or have tons of occult prop in his house, but rather than he merely puts more value on personal conduct than in material stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most hermetics won't do anything to please any cosmic power, since it is stated repeatedly that they don't bow to any superior force and instead force their strong Will upon them. Having said that, how could be the lifestyle of a mage that mixes the 3 practices (High Ritual, Martial arts and Psionics)?<br /> <br /> And are you guys saying that a High Ritual and a Martial artist mage casting effects using hand gestures and energy are visually the same? That what matters is what they do in their everyday life? In this case, are all instruments, used by different practices visualy the same in the moment of the casting??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T11:38:07-07:00","id":1298171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298163#post1298163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how academics, lore or theology has anything to do with meditation, hand gesture, energy and vocalization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classic Hermetic High Ritual works in large part because of the secret knowledge you know. You aren't just meditating, you are meditating on certain specialized forms and symbols, you aren't just gesturing, you are making specifically meaningful gestures. Compare that to martial arts where the meditation might simply be to focus your thoughts and the gestures are to cause specific changes in the flow of energy through your body. The former depends more on esoteric knowledge (academics/lore/theology) the latter depends on your concentration and bodily understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T11:39:19-07:00","id":1298172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298163#post1298163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most hermetics won't do anything to please any cosmic power, since it is stated repeatedly that they don't bow to any superior force and instead force their strong Will upon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mentioned that mostly because Hermetics aren't the only High Ritual mages.<br /> <br /> In the case of Hermetics, their rituals force the powers of the universe to comply by appealing to primordial sacred laws that put humans in charge of the universe. That's what &quot;Will&quot; means to them and that's why it's capitalized. It's not just being headstrong. Let's not ignore the rich mystic background in the first two chapters of the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298171#post1298171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Classic Hermetic High Ritual works in large part because of the secret knowledge you know. You aren't just meditating, you are meditating on certain specialized forms and symbols, you aren't just gesturing, you are making specifically meaningful gestures. Compare that to martial arts where the meditation might simply be to focus your thoughts and the gestures are to cause specific changes in the flow of energy through your body. The former depends more on esoteric knowledge (academics/lore/theology) the latter depends on your concentration and bodily understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much that. Hermetic praxis includes knowing how the cosmos works, what forces need to be cajoled and pushed with your Will to cause an effect. Hermetics do that through the lenses of academics and theology.<br /> <br /> Also Hermetic arrogance it's not quite as careless as rumors would make you believe: Their summoning techniques show their power to impress Umbrood, but note that these beings in particular would accept nothing else (they won't deal with weak mages) and the ritual leaves a chance for the spirit to demand stuff in change of the favor if the Hermetic isn't way more powerful. That isn't a true &quot;binding&quot;, a Spirit 4 forced binding needs not of such concessions. In the fluff you will always see them being polite with powerful beings (not the same as subservient!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having said that, how could be the lifestyle of a mage that mixes the 3 practices (High Ritual, Martial arts and Psionics)?<br /> <br /> And are you guys saying that a High Ritual and a Martial artist mage casting effects using hand gestures and energy are visually the same? That what matters is what they do in their everyday life? In this case, are all instruments, used by different practices visualy the same in the moment of the casting??</div> </div> </div> </div>Visually it may seem the same, yes. How would you know if someone it's meditating to empty the mind or to focus on a tought pattern?.<br /> <br /> But I imagine that your hand gestures are going to be different. They probably came from one or more occult practices, even if refurbished to be usable with kung fu. It would be interesting to determine what beings or impersonal powers are being cajoled with the gestures - someone with high Occult could understand that these gestures make a reference to something.<br /> <br /> I imagine his lifestyle would be very regimented and at the same time academic. Lots of meditation and physical training coupled with lots of occult study. The &quot;three worlds&quot; of Hermeticism: <i>Physical World</i>,<i> Imaginal World </i>and <i>Divine World</i> could get represented by one Practice each, as these represent the elements of the soul.<br /> <br /> Physical mastery would involve a prepared body that can go beyond ordinary limits. The Imaginal World can be related with the hidden potentials of the mind. High Ritual it's related to the Divine and ties to both for the whole <i>&quot;as above so below&quot;</i> vive. Divine in this case it's understood not as an object of worship but as a fact of the world: The &quot;world above&quot; it's not the Umbra <i>per se</i>, but rather the esoteric eternal truth that's behind physical and psychical manifestations of every kind.<br /> <br /> Probably the interest would be to incorporate this &quot;sacred&quot; world (however it looks like) to both Psionics and Martial Arts. You don't just harnes the latent power of your mind, you harness the power of ancient legacies to structure your latent psychic powers - in a sense it's not that different to being a psion that thinks he needs hyperscience helmets to awaken his mind, the difference it's that you use an older (and perhaps harder to notice) approach. In the same vein your Martial Arts are so above the norm becuase your punches have the power of the stars behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-20-2019, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T12:41:15-07:00","id":1298177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298163#post1298163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, the tradition book does have a sidebar about this, only to explain how could an hermetic use his slow casting High Ritual quickly in action situations. But how woul be a ritualistic life of a mage that combine the 3 practices (High Ritual, Martial arts and Psionics)?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking about changing Psionics for Chaos Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would probably go Just Chaos Magick and Martial arts.. between those two you wouldn't Notice High Ritual and I am not even sure a Hermetic could tell where one ends and the other begins at that point.<br /> <br /> The Big difference between the High Ritualist and the Chaos mage is the High Ritualist will believe there's value in the symbolism in and of itself vs the Chaos mage who just believes Belief matters.. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least in the movies, there is not a single spell I can remember that he uses any particular item. </div> </div> </div>The Ring spell off the top of my head, that's without me having to go back and watch the whole movie. There's major plot point that the spell doesn't work without the Rings. Now this could be a Wonder or a Unique Instrament depending on how the player wants to so it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He relies only in hand gestures and energy to cast his spells. I still want to know why his style is considered High Ritual though </div> </div> </div>No he relies upon items and invocations of entities in other realms. You're saying the equivalent of &quot;I don't understand why calling someone on the other side of the planet isn't just hand gestures and energy&quot; which is profoundly misunderstanding how a cellphone works.. or simplifying it to the point of absurdity? Doctor Strange even in the Movies makes heavy use of his &quot;Magical infrastructure&quot; which is really what stuff like High Ritual and Similar magical groupings create. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They know, as most mages too, that magick can be made with Science. But hermetics acknowledge and often study and respect science (low case). My character won't cast his spells using Science, he will just have a logical explanation for what he is doing. It's the internal/external focus thing. He knows that is his enlightened Will channeled through his focus that is doing the effect, and not just the result of using the instruments.<br /> The Psionics were added because it focus in the use of the mage's mind, body and Will to cast effects, which is what my char is going to use, that along with some logical explanation to what he's doing. I think it fits very well. But as I said, I might change for chaos magick, I don;t know.. </div> </div> </div><br /> The Order of Hermes is all about Training wheels. It teaches you hedge magic to convince you that Magic is real. This leads to Awakening. Symbolism with strong mythic threads work to harness the WIll then you surpass things and its Will alone. You don't need to justify Enlightened Will with an Instrament.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, I didn't get what you meant in the second part of this quote. </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference between the finger Gestures of a HIgh Ritualist, or Martial artist, Wierd Scientist or Hypertechnician is less about the particular movement of the Fingers and more the &quot;why&quot; and the broader life style they live in. Someone who combines HIgh Ritual and Martial arts is.. going to be hard to see where one begins and One Ends and I think that's the issue you're hitting here. Doctor Strange, at least in movie combines the two.<br /> <br /> This is what make him look different than say Iron Fist who is ALL martial arts and Harry Potter who's all High Ritual.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most hermetics won't do anything to please any cosmic power, since it is stated repeatedly that they don't bow to any superior force and instead force their strong Will upon them. Having said that, how could be the lifestyle of a mage that mixes the 3 practices (High Ritual, Martial arts and Psionics)? </div> </div> </div>Hermetics never bow to other beings in the same way real world christians are never lacking in Charity or start fights. They fail to live up to their ideals regularly and since they might hold to &quot;Gods and Monsters&quot; as their Paradigm one gets issues.<br /> <br /> However its FAIRLY clear while Practices and Instraments something we can debate about your character they pretty strongly seem to be built on a &quot;Mechanistic cosmos&quot; Paradigm.<br /> <br /> The High Ritualist or Chaos Mage would study different aspects of the supernatural and the beliefs people incorporate into such, he may do little personal rituals when he needs them or draw up his morning Penticle ... just like as a Martial artist he'd spend some time working out to keep in shape. He may combine the two working out while incorporating ritual symbolism.<br /> <br /> Psionics would probably not look MUCH different, he'd work out, meditate use crystals or the right symbols to &quot;grow his mind&quot;<br /> <br /> Remember abstaining from Sex, and or various dietary restrictions are valid Instraments.. these people aren't getting away with Fast casting for free just because at that round of combat you aren't eating a sandwich. They still have to engage in some method of concentration to use their abilities.. more active things like High Ritual or Martial arts just sort of invert the scenario. Its obvious what they are doing in the moment but less obvious what they are doing during their long down times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And are you guys saying that a High Ritual and a Martial artist mage casting effects using hand gestures and energy are visually the same? That what matters is what they do in their everyday life? In this case, are all instruments, used by different practices visualy the same in the moment of the casting?? </div> </div> </div>IT depends how much your pare things down. A Virtual Adept with a super cellphone is just making &quot;hand gestures&quot; across the screen.. a Technocrat who's automated his house is &quot;JUST making verbal invocations&quot; Hand gestures.. cover alot of things through out all of human history. There are particular Mudra in IRL Buddhism that have very different meanings than say American sign Language. IF you want to look up what Western Ritual hand signs look like vs particular martial arts techniques that's what Google's for. You dont' however need this for the game as your character knows the difference even if you as the player do not.. and it doesn't really matter much on a Metalevel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T13:54:36-07:00","id":1298190,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks for the answers. Now I'm thinking about it. Definitely Martial Arts is going to stay, i'd say it's the most important of his practices, but he lacks the serenity, peace of mind and harmony of the spirit that is usual to martial artists mages like the akashics. He uses his martial art and train it to his own use and benefit.<br /> <br /> Psionics were added, as I posted earlier, because of the mind, body and Will aspects of the practice, but maybe this is already covered in the martial arts and might be unecessary. Also it brings the scientific aspect to the char, but this also can be done without taking this practice.<br /> <br /> Now, I need one practice that takes his beliefs away from oriental peacefull and spiritual mindset and brings into more western magick style, focusing in his Will and desire for power. Those are hermetic characteristics, and I was thinking about getting High Ritual to both: fit better into the hermetic tradition and give more of the Will and power hungry thing. The things is, even though my char believes in spirits and unbrood he lacks the material aspects and won't call for any angel, god or demon to cast his effects.<br /> <br /> Another option, as posted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> ,is to use Chaos Magick instead. My char is definitely believes tha Belief matters. This way I could get the Will into his practices and still fit into hermetics a little bit more. <br /> <br /> Since my mage instruments and what he believes were already chosen, I just have to fit the practices into this. For now, it seems tha Martial Arts/Chaos Magick seems the best option, maybe adding Psionics. Does that match hermetic paradigm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T15:34:32-07:00","id":1298205,"title":"","content":"There are Western Martial arts. Quite afew of them. From the strong emphasis on the physical among the Greeks to the litteral breaking of chains in Caopera of course there's also plenty of Eastern Martial arts that don't have anything to say about inner peace(see Mu tai(sp)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T20:27:13-07:00","id":1298262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298205#post1298205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Western Martial arts. Quite afew of them. From the strong emphasis on the physical among the Greeks to the litteral breaking of chains in Caopera of course there's also plenty of Eastern Martial arts that don't have anything to say about inner peace(see Mu tai(sp)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, my char would be a Muay Thai practioner, and the eastern martial arts always have some kind of peaceful teachings. But having only Martial Arts as practice kinda seems odd for the hermetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The difference between the finger Gestures of a HIgh Ritualist, or Martial artist, Wierd Scientist or Hypertechnician is less about the particular movement of the Fingers and more the &quot;why&quot; and the broader life style they live in. Someone who combines HIgh Ritual and Martial arts is.. going to be hard to see where one begins and One Ends and I think that's the issue you're hitting here. Doctor Strange, at least in movie combines the two.<br /> <br /> This is what make him look different than say Iron Fist who is ALL martial arts and Harry Potter who's all High Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post made me think. Iron fist indeed have all the harmony and inner peace that martial artist (like akashics) have. And the main difference between Harry Potter and Dr. Strange is HP uses wands and vocalization while Strange uses gestures (Bases only in the movies). From this I take two points:<br /> <br /> 1) If you didn't see Strange's training in martial arts in Kathmandu and only saw him casting a single spell would you consider him purely High Ritual?<br /> <br /> 2) None of them (HP and Strange) calls from higher beings (like angels, gods, demons) or use any kind of symbolism (like pentagrams, solomon) or even any kind of material (except the wand for HP, or when they brew potions and the like, but that's another practice).<br /> <br /> I'm trying to see how I could fit High Ritual into my char by taking what I can from those sources considered High Ritual.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T06:14:52-07:00","id":1298306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298262#post1298262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) None of them (HP and Strange) calls from higher beings (like angels, gods, demons) or use any kind of symbolism (like pentagrams, solomon) or even any kind of material (except the wand for HP, or when they brew potions and the like, but that's another practice).</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange totally calls from higher beings. This aspect was minimized in the movies but it's a central theme on the comics.<br /> <br /> However, it's important to note that Ritual magick does not need to call for higher <i>beings</i>, merely to a higher <i>powers</i>. And it's only &quot;higher&quot; in the sense that it controls the physical world, it doesn't need to be in a higher &quot;place&quot;. Angels and elementals are a real life example, the stars are other real life example (they aren't Umbrood nor creatures of any kind). Different methaphisics have different &quot;esoteric forces&quot; to conjure.<br /> <br /> In the case of Harry Potter, while it's not very established it's clear that magic follows very strict rules appealing to occult aspects of the world: Wands aren't just lumps of wood, they have a piece of a magical creature inside. Mages themselves are seen as magical creatures with the importance blood has in their society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-21-2019, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T18:23:32-07:00","id":1298449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298262#post1298262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm trying to see how I could fit High Ritual into my char by taking what I can from those sources considered High Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really over thinking this. If you want to play a guy like Doctor Strange as a Hermetic He combines ritual and martial arts into a seamless whole. He will generally be doing finger wiggles when casting in combat, or punching a person with his fast casts. During his down time he's studying magic, working out and possibly has a normal life depending on how you want to run things. When you want to do an extended Ritual.. he does the whole invocation/pentacle things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:01:09-07:00","id":1299414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1298306#post1298306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strange totally calls from higher beings. This aspect was minimized in the movies but it's a central theme on the comics.<br /> <br /> However, it's important to note that Ritual magick does not need to call for higher <i>beings</i>, merely to a higher <i>powers</i>. And it's only &quot;higher&quot; in the sense that it controls the physical world, it doesn't need to be in a higher &quot;place&quot;. Angels and elementals are a real life example, the stars are other real life example (they aren't Umbrood nor creatures of any kind). Different methaphisics have different &quot;esoteric forces&quot; to conjure.<br /> <br /> In the case of Harry Potter, while it's not very established it's clear that magic follows very strict rules appealing to occult aspects of the world: Wands aren't just lumps of wood, they have a piece of a magical creature inside. Mages themselves are seen as magical creatures with the importance blood has in their society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see. I can see my char calling upon forces (non sentient, more like calling the universe) to cast effects. And High Ritual is not only about materials and angels/demons. Having said that, I guess Martial arts with a bit of High Ritual and Chaos Magick is the perfect approach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're really over thinking this. If you want to play a guy like Doctor Strange as a Hermetic He combines ritual and martial arts into a seamless whole. He will generally be doing finger wiggles when casting in combat, or punching a person with his fast casts. During his down time he's studying magic, working out and possibly has a normal life depending on how you want to run things. When you want to do an extended Ritual.. he does the whole invocation/pentacle things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's about right. Except the invocation/pentacle things would more likely be meditation with any combination of the other 6 instruments (and maybe crystals). The Chaos Magick part allows more room for improvisation.<br /> <br /> About the paradigm itself, I read &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot;and I liked a lot. I'm thinking this one as the main, with a bit of &quot;Might is Right&quot; and &quot;Consciousness is the Only True Reality&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:32:34-07:00","id":1299453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1299414#post1299414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see. I can see my char calling upon forces (non sentient, more like calling the universe) to cast effects. And High Ritual is not only about materials and angels/demons. Having said that, I guess Martial arts with a bit of High Ritual and Chaos Magick is the perfect approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, that's about right. Except the invocation/pentacle things would more likely be meditation with any combination of the other 6 instruments (and maybe crystals). The Chaos Magick part allows more room for improvisation.<br /> <br /> About the paradigm itself, I read &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot;and I liked a lot. I'm thinking this one as the main, with a bit of &quot;Might is Right&quot; and &quot;Consciousness is the Only True Reality&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally the advantage of being in a Tradition is the ability to talk shop. Spheres of course allow a common language for the traditions to talk about magic among themselves but broadly each Traditions share certain practices so they can help eachother develop as mages(so to crafts etc) so if you go too far outside the box they may not throw you out but you may not get much out of being a Hermetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:44:43-07:00","id":1299456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1299453#post1299453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Generally the advantage of being in a Tradition is the ability to talk shop. Spheres of course allow a common language for the traditions to talk about magic among themselves but broadly each Traditions share certain practices so they can help eachother develop as mages(so to crafts etc) so if you go too far outside the box they may not throw you out but you may not get much out of being a Hermetic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree, that's why I tried to keep High Ritual. The essence of being a HR and hermetic is that the power comes from the mage's Will. That's for certain is the belief of my mage. Also, the lack of catholic figures such as angels and demons, and material componentes shouldn't keep him from being an hermetic and getting all he can from the tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:35:09-07:00","id":1299473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1299456#post1299456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agree, that's why I tried to keep High Ritual. The essence of being a HR and hermetic is that the power comes from the mage's Will. That's for certain is the belief of my mage. Also, the lack of catholic figures such as angels and demons, and material componentes shouldn't keep him from being an hermetic and getting all he can from the tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you aren't using the same symbols you may agree on principle but get less out of it. As a Chaos mage you can pick up beliefs when you need them. You don't have to have a faith in things in the long term. you can even have faith in things you know are fake..(See Alan Moore and his snake god.. actually just see Alan Moore..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T04:33:53-07:00","id":1299557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1299456#post1299456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agree, that's why I tried to keep High Ritual. The essence of being a HR and hermetic is that the power comes from the mage's Will. That's for certain is the belief of my mage. Also, the lack of catholic figures such as angels and demons, and material componentes shouldn't keep him from being an hermetic and getting all he can from the tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right, because there are several things the Hermetics can talk shop about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> 1) The material components, which your mage will share little of.<br /> 2) The mental components, which your mage may or may not have in common with them. These are things like mental images, shapes, equations, and names.<br /> 3) The theoretical components, which your mage will probably share at least a little of. These are the theoretical underpinnings of the previous two; the reasons why they work.<br /> 4) The metaphysical beliefs, which your character will largely share with them. Why the universe works the way it does. Will as a fundamental part of casting is on this level.<br /> <br /> Having conversations or even debates about 3 and 4 are very rewarding things for someone in the OoH.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T07:27:28-07:00","id":1299590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1293163-choosing-tradition?p=1299557#post1299557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are right, because there are several things the Hermetics can talk shop about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> 1) The material components, which your mage will share little of.<br /> 2) The mental components, which your mage may or may not have in common with them. These are things like mental images, shapes, equations, and names.<br /> 3) The theoretical components, which your mage will probably share at least a little of. These are the theoretical underpinnings of the previous two; the reasons why they work.<br /> 4) The metaphysical beliefs, which your character will largely share with them. Why the universe works the way it does. Will as a fundamental part of casting is on this level.<br /> <br /> Having conversations or even debates about 3 and 4 are very rewarding things for someone in the OoH.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. And I don't think talk talking about magick is the only, nor main, advantage of being in a tradition. Knowing people amd being able to count on people is more important. Or even having access to information via libraries or access to magic items. There are lots of advantages of being in a tradition, and even more in a big ome like the hermetics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}